hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Abd ibn Humayd said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: You recite this verse, {O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strays will not harm you if you are guided}, yet I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If people see the wrongdoer and do not restrain him, Allah will soon envelop them all in His punishment."
"2","Habban ibn Hilal informed me, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq narrated to him, saying: I looked at the feet of the polytheists while we were in the cave and they were above us, and I said, O Messenger of Allah, if one of them were to look at his feet he would see us beneath his feet, so he said: O Abu Bakr, what do you think of two, Allah being the third of them."
"3","Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd, from Aslam al-Kufi, from Murra, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, mighty and majestic, has forbidden Paradise to a body nourished on unlawful means."
"4","Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from al-Mughira ibn Subay, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us: The Dajjal will emerge from a land in the east called Khurasan, followed by peoples whose faces are like hammered shields."
"5","Al-Hasan ibn Musa informed us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication to supplicate with in my prayer, so he said: Say: O Allah, I have wronged myself greatly, and none forgives sins but You, so forgive me with forgiveness from You and have mercy on me; indeed You are the Forgiving, the Merciful."
"6","Yala narrated to us, al-Kalbi narrated to us, from Salama ibn al-Saib, from Abu Rafi, the freedman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: We fell into need, so I took the two anklets of the woman and went out with them in the year in which Abu Bakr was made caliph, and Abu Bakr met me and said, What is this? I said, The two anklets of the woman; the tribe needed expenditure. He said: I have with me silver paper intended for silver. He called for the scale and placed the two anklets in one pan and the silver in the other pan, and the two anklets outweighed by about a daniq, so he cut off the excess. I said, O caliph of the Messenger of Allah, it is lawful for you. He said: O Abu Rafi, even if you deem it lawful, Allah, mighty and majestic, does not make it lawful. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Gold for gold, weight for weight, and silver for silver, weight for weight; the excess and the addition are in the Fire."
"7","Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubayda al-Rabadhi narrated to us, saying: The freedman of Ibn Siba informed me, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar narrating from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when this verse was revealed: {Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it}. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Bakr, shall I not recite to you a verse revealed to me? I said, Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He recited it to me, and I felt as though my back snapped, so that I stretched because of it. The Messenger of Allah said, What is the matter with you, O Abu Bakr? I said, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, which of us has not done evil, and we will surely be recompensed for what we did. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for you, O Abu Bakr, and your fellow believers, you will be recompensed for that in this world, until you meet Allah, mighty and majestic, with no sins upon you; as for the others, it will be gathered for them until they are recompensed for it on the Day of Resurrection."
"8","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that Umar ibn al-Khattab, while he was standing delivering the sermon on Friday, a man from among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, so Umar called out to him, What time is this? He said, I was busy today and did not return to my family until I heard the call, and I did no more than perform ablution. Umar said: And ablution as well, though you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command the ritual bath."
"9","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard me swearing by my father, so he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, forbids you to swear by your fathers. Umar said: By Allah, I never swore by them again, neither deliberately nor by way of transmission."
"10","Abd Allah ibn Yazid informed us, saying: Haywa ibn Shurayh narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Amr informed me that he heard Abd Allah ibn Hubayra, that he heard Abu Tamim al-Jayshani say: that he heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If you were to rely upon Allah with His true reliance, He would provide for you as He provides for the birds; they go out hungry in the morning and return full in the evening."
"11","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Daylam ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Maymun al-Kurdi, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I fear for you only every learned hypocrite who speaks with wisdom but acts with injustice."
"12","Al-Hasan ibn Musa informed us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Lahia narrated to us, saying: al-Dahhak ibn Shurahbil narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution washing once each."
"13","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from Zayd, from his father, from Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take olive oil as condiment and anoint yourselves with it, for it comes from a blessed tree."
"14","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: I heard Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to give charity, and it coincided with wealth I had, so I said, Today I will outstrip Abu Bakr if I ever outstrip him. I brought half my wealth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What have you left for your family? I said, The like of it. And Abu Bakr came with all he had. He said to him: O Abu Bakr, what have you left for your family? He said, I have left for them Allah and His Messenger. I said, I will never compete with you in anything again."
"15","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Yunus ibn Sulayman informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: When revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a sound like the humming of bees would be heard near his face. It descended upon him one day, so we fell silent for a while, then it was lifted from him. He faced the qibla, raised his hands, and said: O Allah, increase us and do not diminish us, honor us and do not disgrace us, give us and do not deprive us, favor us and do not favor others over us, make us pleased and be pleased with us. Then he said: Ten verses have been revealed to me; whoever upholds them will enter Paradise. Then he recited: {The believers have surely succeeded}, until he completed ten verses."
"16","Harun ibn Ismail al-Khazzaz narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Ikrima, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, saying: A visitor from my Lord, mighty and majestic, came to me tonight while I was at al-Aqiq, saying: Pray in this blessed valley, and say, An umra within a hajj."
"17","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Haytham ibn Rafi informed us, saying: Abu Yahya al-Makki narrated to us, from Farrukh, the freedman of Uthman: that Umar went out one day from the mosque and saw food scattered at the door of the mosque, and its abundance pleased him. He said, What is this food? They said, Food brought to us. He said, May Allah bless it and those who brought it to us. One of his companions walking with him said to him, O Commander of the Believers, it has been hoarded. He said, Who hoarded it? They said, So-and-so, the freedman of Uthman, and so-and-so, your freedman. He sent for them and said to them: What drove you to hoard the food of the Muslims? They said, O Commander of the Believers, we buy with our wealth and sell when we wish. Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever hoards food against the Muslims, Allah will strike him with leprosy or bankruptcy. Farrukh said: O Commander of the Believers, I covenant with Allah never to return to dealing in food again, and he turned to dealing in Egyptian cloth. As for the freedman of Umar, he said, O Commander of the Believers, it is our wealth; we buy with it when we wish and sell when we wish. Abu Yahya claimed that he saw the freedman of Umar leprous and deformed."
"18","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Asbagh ibn Zayd informed us, saying: Abu al-Ala informed us, from Abu Umama, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wore a new garment and said: Praise be to Allah who has clothed me with what I cover my nakedness and beautify myself with in my life. Then Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever wears a new garment and says: Praise be to Allah who has clothed me with what I cover my nakedness and beautify myself with in my life, then turns to the garment he has worn out and gives it in charity, will be in the protection of Allah, in the care of Allah, and in the covering of Allah, alive and dead, alive and dead, alive and dead."
"19","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utba, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: When Abd Allah ibn Ubayy died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was called to pray over him. He stood toward him, and when he stood over him intending to pray, I moved until I stood in front of him and said, O Messenger of Allah, over the enemy of Allah, Abd Allah ibn Ubayy, who said on such-and-such day such-and-such, recounting his days. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, until when I pressed him, he said: Step back from me, O Umar; I have been given a choice and I have chosen. It was said to me: {Whether you ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them, even if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them}. If I knew that were I to add to seventy he would be forgiven, I would add. Then he prayed over him and walked with him and stood at his grave until he was finished. Umar said: How strange of me and my daring toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah and His Messenger know best. By Allah, only a short while passed until these two verses were revealed: {And never pray over any of them who dies, nor stand over his grave}, to the end of the verse. After that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never prayed over a hypocrite nor stood over his grave until he passed to Allah, mighty and majestic."
"20","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr al-Aqadi narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, who said: When {Among them are the wretched and the fortunate} was revealed, I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, upon what basis do we act? Upon something already completed, or upon something not yet completed? He said: Rather upon something already completed, O Umar, decreed by the decrees; yet each acts for that for which he was created."
"21","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, saying: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said al-Ansari, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: One day I felt desire and kissed while fasting, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, I have done a grave thing today. He said, What is it? I said, I kissed while fasting. He said, What do you think, if you had rinsed with water? I said, Then it would not harm. He said, Then what is the matter?"
"22","Said ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir say: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab delivering a sermon, mentioning what had befallen people of worldly ease, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) writhing, finding not even poor-quality dates to fill his stomach."
"23","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, that Umar ibn al-Khattab stood at al-Jabiya as a preacher and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us as I stand among you and said: Honor my Companions, for they are the best of you, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then lying will spread, until a man swears an oath without being asked for it and testifies without being asked for it. Whoever delights in the heart of Paradise, let him hold to the community, for Satan is with the solitary one and is farther from two. No man shall be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer."
"24","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Yahya al-Bakka, who said: Abd Allah ibn Umar informed me, saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four rakʿas before noon, after the sun declines, are reckoned like their like in the dawn prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing but that it glorifies Allah at that hour. Then he recited: {Their shadows incline to the right and the left, prostrating}, the whole verse."
"25","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from his brother, from Musab ibn Sad, who said: Hafsa said to her father: Allah has widened provision, so would that you ate softer food than your food and wore softer clothing than your clothing. He said: I will argue against you to yourself. He began reminding her of the condition of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the hardship she had been in, until he made her weep. Then he said: I told you that I had two companions who took a path, and if I take other than their path, I will be taken on other than their path. By Allah, I will share with them their like of life, that I may attain with them their life of ease."
"26","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar kissed the Stone, then said: I know you are a stone, and were I not to have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss you, I would not kiss you."
"27","Sulayman ibn Dawud informed us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, from Abd Allah ibn Uqba al-Hadrami, from Ata ibn Dinar al-Hudhali, from Abu Yazid al-Khawlani, from Fadala ibn Ubayd al-Ansari, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The martyrs are four: a believing man of sound faith who meets the enemy and is true to Allah until he is killed; that is he to whom people raise their eyes on the Day of Resurrection. He raised his head until his cap fell from his head, or from the head of Umar. This is in the first rank. A believing man who, when he meets the enemy, it is as though his skin is struck with the thorns of the talh from cowardice; a stray arrow strikes him and kills him; this is in the second. A believing man who mixed a righteous deed with another evil one, met the enemy and fought until he was killed; this is in the third rank. And a believing man who burdened himself with sins and faults, met the enemy and fought until he was killed; this is in the fourth rank."
"28","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: al-Azhar ibn Sinan informed us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Wasi say: I came to Mecca and met there my brother Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith narrated to me by my father, from my grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said, Yes. He said: Whoever enters one of the markets of the Muslims and says: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; He gives life and causes death, and He is Living and does not die; in His hand is good, and He is over all things capable - Allah writes for him a million good deeds, removes from him a million evil deeds, and raises for him a million degrees. Muhammad said: I came to Khurasan and met Qutayba ibn Muslim and said, I have brought you a gift, and I narrated the hadith to him. He would ride in his procession, come to the market, say it, then leave."
"29","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Umar, who said: The Friday prayer is two rakʿas, the Adha prayer is two rakʿas, the Fitr prayer is two rakʿas, and the travel prayer is two rakʿas, complete without shortening, upon the tongue of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"30","Jafar ibn Awn informed us, saying: Abu Umays informed us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: A man from the Jews came to Umar and said, O Commander of the Believers, a verse in your Book which you recite - had it been revealed upon us, the community of Jews, we would have taken that day as a festival. He said, Which verse? He said: {Today I have perfected for you your religion and completed upon you My favor and approved for you Islam as religion}. Umar said: I know the day in which it was revealed and the place in which it was revealed; it was revealed upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafat on a Friday."
"31","Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami informed us, saying: Ikrima ibn Ammar narrated to us, saying: Abu Zumayl narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Abbas narrated to me, saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to me, saying: On the day of Badr, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the polytheists, who were a thousand, while his Companions were three hundred and nineteen men. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced the qibla, stretched out his hands, and began crying out to his Lord: O Allah, fulfill for me what You promised me; O Allah, where is what You promised me; O Allah, if You destroy this band of the people of Islam, You will never be worshipped on earth. He kept crying out to his Lord, stretching his hands, facing the qibla, until his cloak fell from his shoulder. Abu Bakr came to him, took his cloak, cast it upon his shoulder, then embraced him from behind and said, O Prophet of Allah, your earnest pleading to your Lord suffices; He will surely fulfill for you what He promised you. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {When you sought help from your Lord, He answered you: I will reinforce you with a thousand angels, following one another}. So Allah, mighty and majestic, reinforced him with angels. Abu Zumayl said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me, saying: While a Muslim man was rushing after a polytheist ahead of him, he heard a lash-stroke above him and the voice of a horseman saying, Advance, Hayzum, when he looked at the polytheist ahead of him and he fell flat on his back. He looked at him, and his nose had been bridled and his face split as with a lash-stroke, and all of it turned green. The Ansari came and narrated that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You have spoken truly; that was from the reinforcement of the third heaven. On that day they killed seventy and captured seventy. Abu Zumayl said: Ibn Abbas said: When they captured the captives, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr and Umar, What do you think concerning these captives? Abu Bakr said, O Messenger of Allah, they are sons of uncles and kin; I think you should take ransom from them, that it may be strength for us against the disbelievers, and perhaps Allah will guide them to Islam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, What do you think, O son of al-Khattab? He said, No, by Allah, I do not think what Abu Bakr thinks, O Prophet of Allah; rather I think you should grant us power over them so we strike their necks: grant Ali power over Aqil so he strikes his neck, and grant me power over so-and-so, a kinsman of Umar, so I strike his neck, for these are the leaders of disbelief, its chiefs and commanders. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inclined to what Abu Bakr said and did not incline to what I said. The next day I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with Abu Bakr sitting, weeping. I said, O Messenger of Allah, tell me what you and your companion weep for; if I find weeping I will weep, and if I find no weeping I will feign weeping for your weeping. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I weep for what my Companions proposed to me of taking ransom; their punishment was presented to me nearer than this tree, a tree near the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has thoroughly subdued in the land. You desire the goods of the world, while Allah desires the Hereafter, and Allah is Mighty, Wise. Had it not been for a prior decree from Allah, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took. So eat of what you have taken as lawful and good}. So Allah, mighty and majestic, made the spoils lawful for them."
"32","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: It was said to Umar, Will you not appoint a successor? He said: If I leave it, one better than me has left it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and if I appoint a successor, one better than me has appointed a successor, Abu Bakr."
"33","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, saying: Israil ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ali ibn Salim ibn Thawban [printed as ibn Shawal], who said: Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan narrated to me, saying: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The importer is provided for, and the hoarder is cursed."
"34","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, Yazid ibn al-Had narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Uthman ibn Suraqa, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shades a warrior shall have the like of his reward until he returns or dies, and whoever builds a mosque, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"35","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Husayn ibn Umar narrated to us, Mukhariq narrated to us, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: Some Jews came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Muhammad, is there fruit in Paradise? He said, Yes, in it are fruit, date-palms, and pomegranates. They said, Do they eat as they eat in this world? He said, Yes, and manifold more. They said, Do they relieve themselves? He said, No, but they sweat and perspire, and Allah removes what is in their bellies of harm."
"36","Amr ibn Talha narrated to me, saying: al-Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, who said: One day I swore by my father, when a man behind me said, Do not swear by your fathers. I turned, and behold, it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"37","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi, who said: Abd al-Rahman al-Musalli narrated to me, saying: I heard al-Ashath ibn Qays say: I stayed as a guest with Umar ibn al-Khattab one night and heard him beating his wife. In the morning I said, O Commander of the Believers, concerning what I heard last night of your beating your wife? He said, O Ashath, retain from me three traits I retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do not ask a man for what he beats his family, and do not sleep except upon witr. He said: And I forgot the third."
"38","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, steward of the family of al-Zubayr, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever sees one afflicted with a trial and says: Praise be to Allah who has kept me safe from what He has tried you with and favored me over much of His creation with favor, that trial will not befall him, whatever it be."
"39","Hammad ibn Isa al-Basri narrated to me, saying: Hanzala ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab narrating from his father, from his grandfather, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stretched out his hands in supplication, he would not return them until he wiped his face with them."
"40","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, who said: I vowed a vow in the pre-Islamic age, then asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after I embraced Islam, and he commanded me to fulfill my vow."
"41","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, saying: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A father shall not be killed for his son."
"42","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, saying: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me wealth, and I returned it. When I came to him, he said, What drove you to return what I sent to you? I said, O Messenger of Allah, you told me: It is better for you not to take from people. He said: That was only concerning begging from people; whatever comes to you unsought is but provision Allah, mighty and majestic, has provided you."
"43","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Zakariyya, from Salih ibn Hayy, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsa, then took her back."
"44","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us that he heard Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Labiba narrating from Abu Sinan al-Duali, that he entered upon Umar ibn al-Khattab, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The world is not opened upon anyone but that Allah, mighty and majestic, casts between them enmity and hatred until the Day of Resurrection, and I fear that for you."
"45","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Nubayh, from Aban ibn Uthman, from his father Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: One in ihram shall neither marry nor give in marriage."
"46","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, saying: Hurayth ibn al-Saib narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Hasan say: Humran narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Affan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam has no right in more than these traits: a house to dwell in, a garment to cover his nakedness with, coarse bread, and water."
"47","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ata ibn Farrukh, that Uthman ibn Affan bought land from a man, and the man regretted it and asked him to rescind, so Uthman rescinded for him. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah has admitted to Paradise a man who was easy as seller and buyer, as payer and as claimant."
"48","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, saying: Abu Sinan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab, that Uthman ibn Affan said to Ibn Umar, Judge among people. He said, I will not judge between two men nor lead them in prayer. He said, Your father used to judge. He said, My father used to judge, and if anything was unclear to him he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and if anything was unclear to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he asked Gabriel, and I find none to ask, and I am not like my father. It has reached me that judges are three: a harsh man swayed by caprice, so he is in the Fire; a man who undertakes judging and judges in ignorance, so he is in the Fire; and a man who strives and is correct, so he escapes barely, neither for nor against him. He said: And he said, Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever seeks refuge in Allah has sought a refuge? He said, Yes. He said, I seek refuge in Allah from you, from your making me a judge. So he excused him and said, Do not tell anyone."
"49","Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to me, saying: Imran ibn Hudayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Ubayd, who said: Humran ibn Aban narrated to me, saying: Uthman ibn Affan said, while he seldom narrated from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever knows that prayer is upon him a binding duty, or a prescribed right, will enter Paradise."
"50","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amra, from Uthman ibn Affan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays isha in congregation is as one who stood half the night, and whoever prays fajr in congregation is as one who stood the night."
"51","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, saying: Abu Aqil Zuhra ibn Mabad narrated to me, from Abu Salih, the freedman of Uthman, who said: I heard Uthman ibn Affan upon the minbar say: I had concealed from you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), disliking your dispersal from me; then it occurred to me to narrate it to you, that each man may choose for himself what he will. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Guarding the frontier one day in the path of Allah is better than a thousand days in other stations."
"52","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Ibn Lahia, who said: Musa ibn Wardan narrated to me that he heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say: I heard Uthman ibn Affan upon the minbar say: I would go out, buy dates, measure them into my vessels, then bring them down to the market and say therein such-and-such a measure, take my profit, and leave them with what remained. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: O Uthman, when you buy, measure in full, and when you sell, measure out."
"53","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Umar, from Mukhariq ibn Abd Allah ibn Jabir, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Uthman ibn Affan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cheats the Arabs will not enter my intercession, nor will my love reach him."
"54","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Firas [printed as ibn Umar], from Aban ibn Uthman, from Uthman ibn Affan, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever says in the morning: In the name of Allah, with Whose name nothing harms in the earth nor in the heaven, and He is the Hearing, the Knowing, will be protected until evening; and whoever says it in the evening will be protected until morning."
"55","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, saying: Ibn Ulayya narrated to us, from Khalid, who said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to me, from Humran, from Uthman ibn Affan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies knowing that there is no god but Allah will enter Paradise."
"56","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muslim al-Zuhri narrated to us, from his uncle Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri, who said: Salih ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwa informed me that Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas informed him that he heard Aban ibn Uthman say: Uthman said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: What do you think, if there were a flowing river at the courtyard of one of you, in which he bathes five times each day, what would remain of his dirt? They said, Nothing. He said: Prayers remove sins as water removes dirt."
"57","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Ishaq ibn Said ibn Amr ibn Said ibn al-As narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from his father, who said: I was with Uthman when he called for purification water and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No Muslim man at whom a prescribed prayer arrives, and he perfects its ablution, its humility, and its bowing, but that it is expiation for what preceded it of sins, so long as no major sin is committed, and that throughout all time."
"58","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Shuba, from Jami ibn Shaddad, who said: I heard Humran ibn Aban narrating to Abu Burda, from Uthman, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever completes ablution as Allah commanded him, the prayers are expiations for what is between them."
"59","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, saying: Awf narrated to us, from Mabad al-Juhani, from Humran, who said: I saw Uthman perform ablution, completing it, then laugh. He said, Do you know why I laughed? We said, No. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution, completing it, then laugh and say: Do you know why I laughed? We said, Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: When the Muslim servant performs ablution, completing it, then enters prayer, completing it, he emerges from his sins as his mother bore him."
"60","Muhadir ibn al-Muwarri narrated to me, Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Humran, the freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, from Uthman, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution, perfecting it, then prays, Allah will forgive him what is between it and the next prayer."
"61","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, from Israil, from Uthman ibn Mawhab, who said: Humran ibn Aban said: I was with Uthman when his caller came to announce prayer to him. He said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Bilal came to announce prayer to him. Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended to narrate to you a matter, then it occurred to me to remain silent. We said, O Messenger of Allah, narrate to us; if it is good we will hasten to it, and if it is otherwise we will refrain from it. He said: No Muslim man performs ablution as Allah commanded him, then prays as Allah commanded him, completing bowing and prostration, but that it expiates what preceded it of sin."
"62","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, saying: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Israil narrated to us, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Wail, who said: I saw Uthman ibn Affan perform ablution: he washed his hands thrice, washed his face thrice, rinsed and sniffed thrice, washed his forearms thrice, wiped his head and his ears, their outer and inner, then washed his feet thrice, then ran his fingers through them and through his beard thrice when he washed his face. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as you have seen me do."
"63","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, Amr ibn Murra narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us until he placed his feet between me and Fatima, and taught us what to say when we take our beds: thirty-three glorifications, thirty-three praises, and thirty-four magnifications. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I never abandoned them after. A man said to him, Not even the night of Siffin? He said, Not even the night of Siffin."
"64","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me concerning his sacrificial camels to distribute their meats, skins, and coverings among the poor, and not to give the butcher anything from them, saying: We shall give him the wage from ourselves."
"65","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have exempted for you horses and slaves, so pay the alms of your wealth: from every forty dirhams, a dirham."
"66","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought refuge for the sick, he said: Remove the harm, Lord of people, and heal; You are the Healer; there is no healing but Your healing, leaving no illness."
"67","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Ali, I love for you what I love for myself, and I dislike for you what I dislike for myself: Do not recite while bowing nor while prostrating, do not pray with your hair gathered, for it is the share of Satan; do not squat between the two prostrations, do not fiddle with pebbles, do not prompt the imam, do not wear a gold ring, do not wear qassi garments, do not ride on mayathir, and do not spread your forearms."
"68","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform witr with nine suras of the Mufassal: in the first rakʿa, al-Takathur, Inna Anzalnahu, and Idha Zulzilat; in the second rakʿa, al-Asr, Idha Ja, and Inna Ataynaka al-Kawthar; and in the third rakʿa, Qul Ya Ayyuha al-Kafirun, Tabbat, and Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad."
"69","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not rise until a man from among my Companions is sought as a stray is sought, and is not found."
"70","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damra, from Ali, who said: Witr is not obligatory like prayer, but it is a sunna, so do not abandon it."
"71","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damra, from Ali, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would indeed pray two rakʿas after every prescribed prayer, except asr and fajr."
"72","Said ibn Amir and Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Shuba, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damra, from Ali, who said: From every part of the night the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has performed witr: its beginning, its middle, and its end; and his witr ended at the end of the night."
"73","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shuba informed us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abd Allah ibn Salima: that Ali complained of illness and said: O Allah, if my term has come, grant me rest; if it is a trial, grant me patience; and if it is toward a term, grant me health. Ali said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was saying that and said, How did you say? I repeated the words to him, and he said: O Allah, heal him and grant him health. I was healed, and I never complained of that pain after."
"74","Ibn Abi Shayba informed me, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Salih, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abd Allah ibn Salima, from Ali, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you words which, if you say them, you will be forgiven, though you are already forgiven: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; there is no god but Allah, the High, the Great; glory be to Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the noble Throne; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"75","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from a man, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant believes until he believes in four: he testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, sent with the truth; he believes in the decree; and he believes in the resurrection after death."
"76","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Bishr ibn Numayr informed us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umama, from Ali ibn Abi Talib ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim ibn Abd Manaf, that he would say concerning the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he would say: The bonds of faith are four, and Islam are its followers: the bonds of faith are to believe in Allah alone, and in Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and what he brought; to believe in Allah and know that you will be raised after death; and the establishment of prayer, the giving of alms, the fasting of Ramadan, the pilgrimage to the House, and striving in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"77","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abida, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Trench: What is with them? May Allah fill their graves and houses with fire, as they detained us from the middle prayer until the sun set."
"78","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Said ibn Zayd, brother of Hammad ibn Zayd, informed us, saying: Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from his forefathers, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatima: Rise and witness your sacrifice; for you, with the first drop that falls of its blood, is forgiveness for every past sin. It will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, its meats and bloods, seventyfold, until placed in your scale. Abu Said al-Khudri said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for the family of Muhammad especially, who deserve what they are singled out with apart from others, or for the family of Muhammad and people generally? He said: Rather for the family of Muhammad and people generally."
"79","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Salim ibn Ubayd [printed as Abu Abd Allah] informed us, from Abu Abd Allah, from Abu Jafar, the freedman of Ali ibn Abi Talib, that Ali said one day: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatima: Glorify when you sleep thirty-three times, praise thirty-three times, and magnify thirty-four times; this is a hundred, and it is a thousand good deeds. Whoever says it every night when he sleeps, it is better for him than freeing a slave each night, and for every vein in his body a sin is erased and a good deed written. Ali said: I never abandoned them since I heard Fatima say them to me, not even on the day of Siffin."
"80","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Saba, from Abu Aflah al-Hamdani, from Abd Allah ibn Zurayr al-Ghafiqi, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with gold in one hand and silk in the other and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my community."
"81","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Hisham ibn Amr al-Fazari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Ali: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say at the end of his witr: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You; I cannot enumerate praise upon You; You are as You have praised Yourself."
"82","Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad informed us, saying: Abu Jafar al-Razi informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf made food for us, invited us, and gave us wine to drink. The wine took hold of us, prayer arrived, and they put me forward. I recited: Say, O disbelievers, I do not worship what you worship, and we worship what you worship. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {O you who believe, do not approach prayer while intoxicated until you know what you say}."
"83","Yusuf ibn Buhlul narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Sad ibn Ubayda, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, and Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, each of us a horseman, saying: Go until you come to Rawdat Khakh, for there is a woman from the polytheists with a letter from Hatib ibn Abi Baltaa to the polytheists. We reached her traveling upon her camel where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us. We said, Where is the letter with you? She said, I have no letter. We made her kneel and searched her baggage and found nothing. My two companions said, We see no letter. I said: I know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has not lied; by Him by whom oaths are sworn, you will surely produce the letter or I will strip you. When she saw my resolve, she reached with her hand to her waist-wrapper, girded with a cloak, and produced the letter. We set out with it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What drove you, O Hatib, to what you did? He said: I do not lack faith in Allah and His Messenger, but I wanted to have a favor with the people by which Allah would protect my wealth, for there is none of your Companions there but that he has one by whom Allah protects his family and wealth. He said: He has spoken truly, so say to him only good. Umar ibn al-Khattab said, He has betrayed Allah, His Messenger, and the believers; let me strike his neck. He said: O Umar, what do you know? Perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish, Paradise is assured for you. The eyes of Umar filled with tears, and he said: Allah and His Messenger know best."
"84","Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam informed us, from Mamar, from Mansur, from Sad ibn Ubayda, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: We went out for a funeral, and while we were at al-Baqi, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with a staff in his hand. He came, sat, then scratched the ground with it for a while, then said: There is no living soul but that its place in Paradise or the Fire has been written, and but that it has been written wretched or fortunate. A man said, Shall we not rely upon our writing and abandon action? He said: No, but act; each is eased. As for the people of felicity, they are eased to the action of the people of felicity; as for the people of wretchedness, they are eased to the action of the people of wretchedness. Then he recited: {As for he who gives and fears, and believes in the best, We shall ease him to ease; and as for he who withholds and deems himself free of need, and denies the best, We shall ease him to hardship}."
"85","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala al-Thalabi, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would continue fasting joined to the pre-dawn."
"86","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala al-Thalabi, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ali, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever lies concerning his dream will be tasked with tying a grain of barley on the Day of Resurrection."
"87","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, saying: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Thabit al-Thumali, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfa al-Suwai, who said: We entered upon Ali, who said: Shall I not narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith the believers ought to retain? We said, Yes, O Commander of the Believers. He narrated to us, and when we left we forgot it. We returned to him, and he recited this verse: {Whatever misfortune befalls you is for what your hands earned, and He pardons much}. Whatever sin Allah has punished in this world, Allah, mighty and majestic, is too forbearing to double its punishment in the Hereafter; and whatever sin Allah has pardoned in this world, Allah is too generous to return upon His pardon."
"88","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: Ali ibn Rabia informed us: that he witnessed Ali when he mounted; when he placed his foot in the stirrup he said, In the name of Allah; when he settled he said, Praise be to Allah. Then he said: {Glory to Him who subjected this to us, and we were not capable of it, and indeed to our Lord we shall return}. Then he praised thrice and magnified thrice, then said: There is no god but You; I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You. Then he laughed. It was said, What makes you laugh, O Commander of the Believers? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as I did and say as I said, then laugh. We said, What makes you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The servant - or he said: I marvel at the servant - when he says: There is no god but You; I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You; he knows that none forgives sins but He."
"89","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Ali ibn Rabia, who said: I was riding behind Ali, and when he placed his foot in the stirrup he said, In the name of Allah; when he settled upon the saddle he said, Praise be to Allah. Then he said: {Glory to Him who subjected this to us, and we were not capable of it}, the verse. Then he said: Praise be to Allah, praise be to Allah, praise be to Allah, thrice; Allah is greatest, Allah is greatest, Allah is greatest, thrice. Then he said: Glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah, thrice. Then he said: There is no god but You, glory be to You; I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You. Then he laughed. I said, What did you laugh at, O Commander of the Believers? He said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did as you saw me do, then laughed. I said, What did you laugh at, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I marvel at our Lord; He marvels at His servant when he says: Forgive me my sins, for none forgives sins but You. He said: My servant knows he has no lord but Me."
"90","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah al-Ashjai narrated to me, from Sufyan ibn Said, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira al-Thaqafi, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Ali ibn Alqama al-Anmari, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: When {O you who believe, when you confer privately with the Messenger, offer charity before your private conference} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: What do you think, a dinar? I said: They cannot bear it. He said, Then how much? I said: A barley-grain. He said: You are indeed austere. Then was revealed: {Are you afraid to offer charities before your private conference}, the verse. Through me Allah lightened it for this community."
"91","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perfecting ablution amid hardships, walking on foot to the mosques, and awaiting prayer after prayer wash away sins thoroughly."
"92","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Abu Sinan al-Duali Yazid ibn Umayya, who said: Ali fell ill with an illness we feared for him, then he recovered and regained health. We said: Praise be to Allah who has healed you, O Commander of the Believers; we had feared for you in this illness of yours. He said: But I did not fear for myself. The truthful, believed one narrated to me, saying: You shall not die until this of you is struck, meaning his head, and this is dyed with blood, meaning his beard, and the most wretched of them kills you, as the most wretched of so-and-so's tribe hamstrung the she-camel of Allah; he singled him to his thigh: the world apart from Thamud."
"93","Abu Nuaym and Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayra, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake his family in the last ten of Ramadan."
"94","Yala narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, and I said, O Messenger of Allah, you send me while I am young to judge among them, and I do not know judging? He struck my chest with his hand and said: O Allah, guide his heart and make his tongue firm. He said: By Him who split the seed, I never doubted after in judging between two."
"95","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Mukhtar ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Abu Matar, who said: While we were sitting with the Commander of the Believers in the mosque at the door of al-Rahba with the Muslims, a man came to Ali and said: Show me the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at midday. He called Qanbar and said, Bring me a cup of water. He washed his hands and face thrice, inserted some of his fingers into his mouth, sniffed thrice, washed his forearms thrice, wiped his head once, then said, meaning the ears: their outer is of the head and their inner is of the face; and his feet to the ankles, his beard dripping upon his chest. Then he sipped a sip after ablution, then said: Where is the asker about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Such was the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"96","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Mukhtar ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Abu Matar, who said: I came out of the mosque when a man called from behind me: Raise your waist-wrapper, for it is cleaner for your garment and more godfearing for you, and take from your head if you are a Muslim. I walked behind him while he was before me, wrapped in a waist-wrapper, cloaked in a cloak, with a stick, as though a desert Bedouin. I said, Who is this? A man said to me, I see you are a stranger in this town? I said, Yes, a man from Basra. He said, This is Ali, the Commander of the Believers. He proceeded until he reached the house of Banu Abi Muayt, the camel market, and said: Sell and do not swear, for oaths sell goods but efface blessing. Then he came to the date-sellers, and a servant-girl was weeping. He said, What makes you weep? She said, This man sold me dates for a dirham, but my masters returned them and he refuses to accept them. Ali said to him, Take your dates and give her her dirham, for she has no authority. He repelled him, so I said, Do you know who this is? He said, No. I said, This is Ali, the Commander of the Believers. He poured out his dates and gave her her dirham. He said, I would love that you be pleased with me, O Commander of the Believers. He said: What pleases me concerning you is when you fulfill their rights. Then he passed by the date-sellers and said, O date-sellers, feed the poor; your earnings will increase. Then he passed on with the Muslims until he reached the fish-sellers and said, No floating dead fish shall be sold in our market. Then he came to Dar Furat, the cloth market, and came to an old man and said, O old man, sell me well a shirt for three dirhams. When he recognized him he would not buy from him. Then he came to another, and when he recognized him he would not buy from him. He came to a young boy and bought from him a shirt for three dirhams, wearing it between the wrists and the ankles, saying as he wore it: Praise be to Allah who has provided me of adornment what I beautify myself with among people and cover my nakedness with. It was said to him, O Commander of the Believers, is this something you narrate from yourself or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Rather something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at clothing. The father of the boy, owner of the garment, came, and it was said to him, O so-and-so, your son today sold the Commander of the Believers a shirt for three dirhams. He said, Would that you had taken two dirhams from him. His father took a dirham, then brought it to the Commander of the Believers while he was sitting with the Muslims at the door of al-Rahba and said, Keep this dirham. He said, What is this dirham? He said, Our shirt was worth two dirhams. He said: He sold me with his consent and took with his consent."
"97","Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, who said: Yaish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham narrated to me, saying: It was narrated from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam that it was narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There has crept to you the disease of the nations before you: envy and hatred, and hatred is the shaver. I do not say it shaves hair, but it shaves religion. Then he said: By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Then he said: Shall I not tell you of a matter which, if you do it, you will love one another? They said, What is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Spread peace among you."
"98","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, saying: Ibn Numayr and Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to me, from Musa ibn Ubayda, from Muhammad ibn Thabit, from Abu Hakim, the freedman of al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No morning dawns upon the servants but that a caller calls: Glorify the King, the Holy."
"99","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, saying: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat supplicating, he placed his right palm upon his right thigh, pointed with his index finger, placed his thumb upon his middle finger, placed his left hand upon his left thigh, and fitted his left palm to his knee."
"100","Husayn al-Jufi and Abu al-Walid narrated to us, from Zaida, from Simak, from Musa ibn Talha, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Let one of you place before him like the back of a saddle, then pray."
"101","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Musa ibn Talha, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices one of you to have before him like the back of a saddle; whatever passes before him will not harm him."
"102","Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Simak, from Musa ibn Talha, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people atop date-palms and said, What are these doing? He said: They pollinate, placing the male into the female, so it is pollinated. He said, I do not think that avails anything. They were told of that and abandoned it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told, so he said: If it benefits them, let them do it; I merely opined an opinion, so do not hold me to opinion. But when I tell you something from Allah, mighty and majestic, take it, for I have never lied concerning Allah, mighty and majestic, at all."
"103","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Sufyan narrated to us, from Bilal ibn Yahya ibn Talha ibn Ubayd Allah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the crescent he said: O Allah, bring it upon us with felicity and faith, safety and Islam; my Lord and your Lord is Allah."
"104","Ibn Abi Shayba narrated to me, saying: Waki narrated to us, from Talha ibn Yahya, who said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talha narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, who said: Three men from Banu Udhra came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and embraced Islam. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Who will undertake these for me? Talha said, I will. They stayed with me. An expedition was announced among people, and one of them went out in it and was martyred. They remained as Allah willed, then another was announced and the second went out in it and was martyred. The third remained until he died upon his bed. Talha said: I saw in sleep as though I was admitted to Paradise and saw them, recognizing them by their lineages and marks; the one who died upon his bed entered first of them, then the second of the martyrs after him, and the first of them was last of them. That troubled me, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None is more excellent with Allah, mighty and majestic, than a believer who lives long in Islam for his magnifying, praising, glorifying, and declaring Allah one."
"105","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Talha ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl, from Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever wrongfully takes a span of land will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."
"106","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ubayda ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar, from Talha ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, from Said ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed defending his religion is a martyr, whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr, whoever is killed defending his blood is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his family is a martyr."
"107","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ward ibn Thumama, from al-Lajlaj, from Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man saying: O Allah, I ask You patience. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have asked Allah for trial, so ask Him well-being. He passed by a man saying: O Allah, I ask You the perfection of favor. He said: O son of Adam, do you know what perfection of favor is? He said, O Messenger of Allah, a supplication I supplicated hoping for good. He said: Perfection of favor is entry into Paradise and deliverance from the Fire. He passed by a man saying: O Possessor of majesty and honor. He said: You have been answered, so ask."
"108","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid informed us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr and Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadramis, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The judge in his judgment descends into a slippery place farther than Aden, most evident in Hell."
"109","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Baqiyya informed us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Campaigning is two campaignings: as for whoever seeks thereby the face of Allah, obeys the commander, spends the precious, treats the partner gently, and avoids corruption, his sleep and wakefulness are all reward; and as for whoever campaigns for boast, show, and repute, disobeys the commander, and corrupts in the land, he will not return even even."
"110","Husayn al-Jufi - that is ibn Ali - narrated to us, from Zaida, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who met a woman with no acquaintance between them, and there is nothing a man does with his wife but that he did it with her, except that he did not have intercourse with her? Then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in watches of the night; good deeds remove evil deeds; that is a reminder for the mindful}. He commanded him to perform ablution and pray. Muadh said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, is it for him especially or for the believers generally? He said: Rather for the believers generally."
"111","Husayn al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaida, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: Two men reviled one another before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of them grew intensely angry, until it seemed his nose was writhing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know a word which, if this angry one said it, his anger would leave him: I seek refuge in Allah, the Hearing, the Knowing, from Satan the accursed. He said: writhing, meaning as though bursting from severity of anger."
"112","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Mamar informed us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abu Wail, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and one morning I was near him while we traveled. I said, O Prophet of Allah, tell me of an action that admits me to Paradise and distances me from the Fire. He said: You have asked about a great matter, yet it is easy for whom Allah eases it: You worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give alms, fast the month of Ramadan, and pilgrimage to the House. Then he said: Shall I not guide you to the doors of good? Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and a man's prayer in the depth of night. Then he recited: {Their sides forsake}. Then he said: Shall I not tell you of the head of the matter, its pillar, and the peak of its hump? I said, Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The head of the matter is Islam, its pillar is prayer, and the peak of its hump is striving. Then he said: Shall I not tell you of the control of all that? I said, Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He took hold of his tongue and said: Restrain this upon you. I said, O Messenger of Allah, shall we indeed be taken to account for what we speak? He said: May your mother bereave you, O Muadh; does anything cast people into the Fire upon their faces - or upon their nostrils - on the Day of Resurrection but the harvests of their tongues."
"113","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram, who said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm narrated to me, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, no face grows pale nor foot grows dusty in an action seeking the ranks of Paradise after the prescribed prayer like striving in the path of Allah; nor does a servant's scale weigh heavy like an animal that perishes for him in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic, or is ridden in the path of Allah."
"114","Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Iyad, from Aban, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan is the wolf of the son of Adam, like the wolf of sheep; the wolf of sheep takes the lean and the stray of the sheep, and does not enter the congregation. So hold to the generality, the congregation, and the mosques."
"115","Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Amir al-Aslami, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge in Allah from craving that leads to ingrained avarice, from craving for that in which there is no prospect, and from craving where there is no ground for craving."
"116","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muadh: O Muadh. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Muadh. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Muadh. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Give glad tidings to the people; whoever testifies that none is worthy of worship but Allah will enter Paradise."
"117","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shubah narrated, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says at the time of death, sincerely: None is worthy of worship but Allah, will enter Paradise."
"118","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated, he said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar al-Makki, he said: Jabir ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated, he said: Muadh ibn Jabal said in his illness: Were it not that you would rely upon it, I would narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Whoever dies with None is worthy of worship but Allah in his heart, with certainty, will enter Paradise."
"119","Abu Asim al-Nabil informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa narrated, he said: Malik ibn Yukhamir narrated, he said: Muadh ibn Jabal narrated that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fights in the path of Allah for the time between two milkings of a she-camel, from a Muslim man, Paradise becomes due for him. Whoever sincerely asks Allah within himself for martyrdom will have the like of the reward of a martyr. Whoever is wounded with a wound in the path of Allah or suffers a mishap in the path of Allah, it will come forth as copious as it ever was, its colour like saffron and its scent like musk. Whoever is wounded in the path of Allah will bear upon him the seal of the martyrs."
"120","Abdillah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, from Uqbah ibn Muslim, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from al-Sunabihi, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand one day and said: O Muadh, indeed I love you for the sake of Allah. Muadh said: May my father and mother be ransomed for you; by Allah, indeed I love you. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Muadh, do not omit to say after every prayer: O Allah, help me to remember You, to thank You, and to worship You excellently. And Muadh enjoined that upon al-Sunabihi, and al-Sunabihi enjoined it upon Abu Abd al-Rahman, and Abu Abd al-Rahman enjoined it upon Uqbah ibn Muslim."
"121","Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Tawus, from Muadh, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no divorce for one who has not married, no emancipation for one who does not own, and no vow in disobedience to Allah."
"122","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Muadh ibn Jabal: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the expedition of Tabuk, and he would not depart at midday until it had cooled, and he would combine Zuhr and Asr; then in the evening he would combine Maghrib and Isha."
"123","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil ibn Yunus, from Yahya, from Ubaydullah ibn Muslim al-Hadrami, from Muadh, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There are no two Muslims who lose three children except that Allah admits their parents, meaning Paradise, by the bounty of His mercy. They said: Or two, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Or two. They said: Or one, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Indeed the miscarried foetus drags its mother by its umbilical cord to Paradise."
"124","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Shubah narrated, he said: Abu Awn informed me, from al-Harith ibn Amr, the brother of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, from the companions of Muadh among the people of Hims, from Muadh: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to Yemen, he said to him: How will you judge when a case presents itself to you? He said: I will judge by what is in the Book of Allah. He said: And if it is not in the Book of Allah? He said: Then by the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And if it is not in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah? He said: I will exercise my own reasoning, sparing no effort. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his chest and said: Praise be to Allah who has granted the messenger of the Messenger of Allah success in what pleases the Messenger of Allah."
"125","Al-Qanabi narrated to us, Malik narrated, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Idris, from Muadh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: My love is due for those who love one another for My sake, who visit one another for My sake, who spend upon one another for My sake, and who sit together for My sake."
"126","Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah informed, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Zabyah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who sleeps while remembering Allah, mighty and majestic, in a state of purity, then wakes in the night and asks Allah for good of this world and the Hereafter, except that He gives it to him. Hammad said: Thabit al-Bunani said: Abu Zabyah came to us and narrated to us this hadith."
"127","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Tawus, from Muadh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam has performed no deed more saving for him from the Fire than the remembrance of Allah, mighty and majestic. They said: O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad in the path of Allah? He said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah, unless you strike with your sword until it breaks, then strike with it until it breaks; he said it three times."
"128","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Razin, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Shall I not guide you to a gate among the gates of Paradise? He said: And what is it? He said: There is no power and no strength except through Allah."
"129","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Muawiyah narrated, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from al-Harith ibn Umayr al-Zubayri, who said: The plague broke out in Sham, so Muadh stood among the people in Hims and addressed them, saying: This plague is the mercy of your Lord, the invocation of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you."
"130","The Musnad of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him. Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Salim ibn Ubayd informed, from Abu Abdillah, from Muhammad ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: For every Muslim there are three things: there is no Muslim man who shoots an arrow in the path of Allah at the enemy, whether it hits or misses, except that the reward of that arrow is for him like the emancipation of a soul; there is no Muslim man a grey hair of whom turns white in the path of Allah except that it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection shining before him; and there is no Muslim man who frees a young or an old slave except that it is binding upon Allah to recompense him manifold for every limb of him."
"131","Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Israil narrated, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas: The idolaters said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Drive these away from us lest they grow bold against us. There were four of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there occurred in his mind whatever Allah willed should occur, so this verse was revealed: {And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening} to the end of the verse."
"132","Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Shubah narrated, from Simak, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, who said: Four verses were revealed concerning me. He said: My mother swore she would eat no food and drink no drink until I disbelieved in Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When we wanted to feed her, we would take a stick and insert it into her mouth, and pour food and drink into her mouth; so this verse was revealed concerning me: {And We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents} up to His saying: {But if they strive to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge}. He said: We were drinking, and we boasted; so I boasted against a man of the Ansar, and he lifted the jawbone of a camel and struck my nose with it, splitting it; so the nose of Sad was split. He said: Then the prohibition of wine was revealed concerning me. He said: I acquired a sword on the day of Badr, and I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, grant it to me as spoils. He said: Put it down. He said: I said: Do not make one who has fought valiantly like one who has no valour. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put it down. Then was revealed: {They ask you about the spoils of war}. He said: And the verse of bequests was revealed concerning me."
"133","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I fell ill with an illness from which I feared death. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth and none inherits from me except a daughter of mine; shall I bequeath two thirds of my wealth? He said: No. I said: Then half of my wealth? He said: No. I said: Then a third of my wealth? He said: A third, and a third is much. Indeed, O Sad, if you leave your heirs rich it is better for you than leaving them dependent, begging from people. Indeed, O Sad, you will never spend an expenditure seeking thereby the Face of Allah except that you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you lift to the mouth of your wife. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind after my companions? He said: If you are left behind and perform a deed seeking thereby the Face of Allah, mighty and majestic, you will only increase thereby in rank and elevation; and perhaps you will be left behind so that Allah benefits some people through you and harms others through you. O Allah, complete for my Companions their emigration, and do not turn them back on their heels. But the unfortunate Sad ibn Khawlah - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pitied him, for he had died in Makkah."
"134","Jafar narrated to us, Musa al-Juhani narrated, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to those sitting with him: Is any one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds in a day? They said: How can any one of us earn a thousand good deeds in a day? He said: He glorifies Allah a hundred times, so a thousand good deeds are recorded for him thereby, and a thousand sins are removed from him thereby."
"135","Said ibn Amir narrated to us, from Shubah, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Sad and Abu Bakrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever claims sonship to a father other than his own father, while knowing he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden to him."
"136","Jafar informed us, Musa al-Juhani informed, from Musab, from his father, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me words to say. He said: Say: None is worthy of worship but Allah, alone, without partner; Allah is Most Great, greatly; praise be to Allah abundantly; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; and there is no power and no strength except through Allah, the Mighty, the Wise. He said: This is for my Lord, so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me well-being, and provide for me."
"137","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated, from Ibn Labibah, from Sad, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best remembrance is the hidden, and the best provision is what suffices."
"138","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Umar ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: Sad ibn Abi Waqqas narrated, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fighting a Muslim is disbelief, and reviling him is wickedness, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days."
"139","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Umar ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I marvel at the believer; if good befalls him he praises Allah, mighty and majestic, and gives thanks, and if a calamity befalls him he praises Allah and is patient. So the believer is rewarded in every matter of his, even rewarded for the morsel he lifts to the mouth of his wife."
"140","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave to some men and did not give anything to one man among them. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave so-and-so and so-and-so and did not give so-and-so, though he is a believer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or a Muslim - he said it three times. Al-Zuhri said: So we consider Islam to be the word and faith to be the deed."
"141","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the killing of the gecko and called it a little wicked one."
"142","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated, from Hakim ibn Abdillah, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says when he hears the call to prayer: And I bear witness that none is worthy of worship but Allah, alone, without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger; I am pleased with Allah as Lord and with Muhammad as Prophet - his sin is forgiven. I said: What preceded of his sin? He said: Not so; Sad said: He said: His sin is forgiven."
"143","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shubah narrated, Abu Ishaq narrated, I heard al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth narrating from Umar ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I marvel at the Muslim; if good befalls him he praises Allah, mighty and majestic, and gives thanks, and if a calamity befalls him he considers it for reward and is patient. Indeed the Muslim is rewarded in everything, even the morsel he lifts to his mouth."
"144","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrimi narrated, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salaam to his right, the whiteness of his left cheek could be seen, and when he gave salaam to his left, the whiteness of his right cheek could be seen."
"145","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Musab narrated, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar, he said: Some people came out from the presence of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz and reported that Amir ibn Sad said: I heard my father say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats seven dates between the two lava plains of Madinah, no poison will harm him that day until night."
"146","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Musab ibn Sad, from Sad, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people are most severely tried? He said: The Prophets, then the next best, then the next best. A man is tried according to his religion; if there is firmness in his religion, firmness is increased, and if there is softness in his religion, it is lightened for him. And trial does not cease with the servant until he walks upon the earth with no sin upon him."
"147","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from Sad, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the pledge from the women, a woman stood up to him as though she were from the women of Mudar and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a burden upon our fathers, our sons, and our husbands, so what is lawful for us of their wealth? He said: The fresh produce; you may eat of it and give of it as a gift."
"148","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated, from Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi, from Abdillah ibn Ubaydah, from the daughter of Sad, from her father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and the nights and days will not pass until my nation splits into the like of them, or he said: into the like of that; and every sect among them is in the Fire except one, and it is the congregation."
"149","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih al-Tammar narrated to me, from Sad ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Amir ibn Sad narrating from his father, who said: When Sad ibn Muadh judged concerning Banu Qurayzah that those upon whom the razor had passed be killed, and that their wealth and offspring be divided, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has judged among them today with the judgement of Allah, mighty and majestic, which He decreed above the seven heavens."
"150","Abdillah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Kathir, that Sad ibn Abi Waqqas came seeking repayment of a debt owed to him by a man, and they said: He has gone out. He said: Then I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If a man is killed in the path of Allah, then brought back to life, then killed, then brought back to life, then killed, he will not enter Paradise until he settles his debt."
"151","Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated, he said: Abdillah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated, from Abdillah ibn Abi Nahik, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not recite the Quran in a melodious voice."
"152","Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Asim ibn Bahdalah informed, from Musab ibn Sad ibn Malik, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl and ate from it, and a remainder remained. He said: A man will come from this mountain path, from the people of Paradise, who will eat this remainder. Sad said: I had left my brother Umayr performing ablution, and I said: It is Umayr. He said: Then Abdillah ibn Salam came and ate it."
"153","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I declare sacred what is between the two lava plains of Madinah, that its thorny trees be cut or its game be killed. And he said: Madinah is better for them if they only knew; none leaves it out of dislike for it except that Allah replaces in it one better than him, and none remains steadfast upon its hardship and strain except that I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"154","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, he said: Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated, from Badr ibn Uthman, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sad narrated to me, from Umar ibn Sad, from Sad, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You are testified as martyrs by killing, plague, drowning, abdominal illness, and the death of a woman dying in childbirth, her death in her confinement."
"155","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim ibn Sad, from Sad ibn Malik, Usamah ibn Zayd, and Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This plague is a filth and the remainder of a punishment with which a people were punished; so if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it fleeing from it, and if it occurs in a land and you are not in it, do not enter it."
"156","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated, from Abdillah ibn Jafar, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant prostrates, he prostrates upon seven bones: his face, his two hands, his two knees, and his two feet; whatever he fails to place, he has diminished."
"157","The Musnad of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with him. Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Bajali narrated to me, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, he said: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to me, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah al-Ansari, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I met Gabriel, peace be upon him, and he gave me glad tidings, saying: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, says to you: Whoever sends blessings upon you, I send blessings upon him, and whoever greets you with peace, I greet him with peace. So I prostrated to Allah in gratitude."
"158","Habban ibn Hilal narrated to me, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated, al-Nadr ibn Shayban narrated, he said: I met Abu Salamah and said: Narrate to me a hadith you heard from your father, which your father heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with no one between you and him. He said: My father narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, has made the fasting of Ramadan obligatory, and I have instituted its standing in prayer; so whoever fasts it and stands it in faith and seeking reward will emerge from sins as on the day his mother bore him."
"159","Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, he said: A storyteller from the people of Palestine narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things - by the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I would indeed swear upon them: wealth is not diminished by charity, so give charity; no servant pardons an injustice, seeking thereby the Face of Allah Almighty, except that Allah raises him thereby in honour on the Day of Resurrection; and no servant opens for himself a door of begging except that Allah opens for him a door of poverty."
"160","Ibn Abi Fudayk informed me, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed me, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from Nawfal ibn Iyas al-Hudhali, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf was a companion of ours, and what an excellent companion; one day he turned back with us until he brought us into his house, then entered and bathed, then came out and sat with us, and we were brought a platter containing bread and meat. When it was set down, Abd al-Rahman wept. So I said to him: O Abu Muhammad, what makes you weep? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and neither he nor the people of his household ever ate their fill of barley bread; so I do not see us as having been kept back except for what is better for us."
"161","The narration of Ubayy ibn Kab, may Allah be pleased with him. Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: There was a man - I know of no one among the people of Madinah who prayed toward the qiblah whose house was farther from the mosque than his - and he used to attend prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So it was said to him: If only you would buy a donkey to ride in the heat and the darkness. He said: By Allah, it would not please me for my house to be adjacent to the mosque. That was reported to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he asked him about that. He said: O Messenger of Allah, so that my footsteps, my going and my returning to my family, my coming and my going, may be recorded - or as he said. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has granted you all of that, and given you all that you hoped for - or as he said."
"162","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sufyan al-Thawri informed, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who said: I went out with Zayd ibn Suhan and Salman ibn Rabiah, and I found a whip and took it. They said: Leave it. I said: I will not leave it for the beasts; I shall take it and benefit from it. So I asked Ubayy ibn Kab, and he said: You did well. I found a purse containing a hundred dinars in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I brought it to him. He said: Announce it for a year. So I announced it for a year and found no one who recognised it, then I came to him. He said: Announce it for another year. Then I came to him, and he said: Announce it for another year. Then he said: Count its number, its string, and its container; then if its seeker comes and informs you of its number, its string, and its container, hand it to him, otherwise benefit from it."
"163","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sufyan informed, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said: I came to Ubayy ibn Kab and said: O Abu al-Mundhir, what do you say concerning the Night of Decree, for Abdillah says: Whoever stands the whole year will attain it? He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman; indeed he knows it is in Ramadan and that it is the night of the twenty-seventh, but it has been obscured from many people lest they rely upon it. By the One who sent down the Book upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), indeed it is in Ramadan, and indeed it is the night of the twenty-seventh. He said: I said: O Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us of, which we memorised and counted; by Allah, indeed it is it, without exception. He said: I said to Zirr: And what is the sign he mentioned? The sun rises that morning as though a basin, with no rays."
"164","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Humayd al-Tawil informed, from Anas ibn Malik, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: A man recited a verse, while I had recited it differently. So I said: Who taught you this? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught it to me. So I set out with him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you teach me such-and-such verse? He said: Yes. Then the man said: Did you teach me such-and-such verse? He said: Yes. Then he said: Gabriel and Mikael came to me; Gabriel sat on my right and Mikael on my left. Gabriel said: O Muhammad, recite the Quran upon one letter. Mikael said: Ask for more. So I said: Give me more. He said: Recite it upon two letters. Mikael said: Ask for more. So I said: Give me more. He said: Recite it upon three letters. Mikael said: Ask for more. So I said: Give me more; thus until it reached seven letters, Gabriel each time saying to him: Recite, and Mikael saying: Ask for more, until it reached seven letters. Then he said: Recite it upon seven letters, each sufficient and healing."
"165","Abu Usamah informed me, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar al-Ansari, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub al-Huraqi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not teach you a surah, the like of which was never revealed in the Torah, nor in the Psalms, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Quran? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Perhaps you will not leave that door until I inform you of it. He said: So I stood with him, and he began speaking to me while my hand was in his, and I began to slow down, disliking that he should leave before informing me of it. When I drew near the door, I said: O Messenger of Allah, the surah you promised me. He said: How do you recite when you stand in prayer? So I recited the Opening of the Book. He said: It is it, and it is the seven oft-repeated verses which Allah, mighty and majestic, mentioned: {And We have certainly given you seven of the oft-repeated and the great Quran}; it is that which I have been given."
"166","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Amir al-Aslami narrated, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Sahl ibn Sad, from Ubayy ibn Kab: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the mosque founded upon piety, and he said: It is my mosque."
"167","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shubah narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Dharr, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Kab: that the wind raged in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man reviled it. He said: Do not revile it, for it is commanded; rather say: O Allah, I ask You for its good, the good within it, and the good it has been commanded with, and I seek refuge in You from its evil, the evil within it, and the evil it has been commanded with."
"168","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning His saying, mighty and majestic: {And remind them of the days of Allah} - he said: By the blessings of Allah."
"169","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil ibn Yunus, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas - and we were with him - and the people said: Nawf al-Shami claims that the one who went seeking knowledge was not Musa of the Children of Israel. Ibn Abbas was reclining, then sat upright and said: Is that so, O Said ibn Jubayr? I said: I myself heard him say that. Ibn Abbas said: Nawf has lied. Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to me that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The mercy of Allah upon us and upon Musa; had he not hastened, felt shy, and been seized by embarrassment before his companion - for he said to him: If I ask you about anything after it, then do not keep me in your company - he would have seen wonders from his companion. He said: And when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a prophet among the prophets, he would begin with himself, saying: The mercy of Allah upon us and upon Salih; the mercy of Allah upon us and upon the brother of Ad. Then he said: Musa, peace be upon him, while he was addressing his people one day, said to them: There is no one on earth more knowledgeable than I. So Allah Almighty revealed to him that there is on earth one more knowledgeable than you, and the sign of that is that you take provision of a salted fish; when you lose it, he is where you lose it. So he took provision of a salted fish, and set out, he and his lad, until when they reached the place they had been commanded, and when they arrived at the rock, Musa went off seeking, and his lad placed the fish upon the rock; it stirred and took its way into the sea, slipping away. His lad said: When the Prophet of Allah comes I shall tell him, but Satan made him forget. Then they set out, and there befell them what befalls the traveller of fatigue and weariness - and what befalls the traveller of fatigue and weariness had not befallen him until he passed beyond what he had been commanded - so Musa said to his lad: {Bring us our morning meal; we have certainly suffered in this journey of ours much fatigue}. His lad said to him: O Prophet of Allah, {Did you see when we retired to the rock, indeed I forgot the fish} to tell you, {and none made me forget it except Satan} {so it took its way into the sea, slipping away}. He said: That is what we were seeking. So they returned upon their footsteps, retracing, until they reached the rock; he circled it, and there he was, wrapped in a garment. He greeted him, and he raised his head and said: Who are you? He said: Musa. He said: Which Musa? He said: Musa of the Children of Israel. He said: What is your affair? He said: I have been told you possess knowledge, so I wished to accompany you. He said: {Indeed, you will never be able to have patience with me}. He said: {You will find me, if Allah wills, patient, and I will not disobey you in any order}. He said: How can you be patient over what you do not comprehend? He said: I have been commanded to do it; you will find me, if Allah wills, patient. He said: {Then if you follow me, do not ask me about anything until I mention it to you}. So they set out until, when they boarded the ship, those aboard it disembarked, and he stayed behind to bore a hole in it. Musa said to him: Do you bore a hole in it to drown its people? You have certainly done a grave thing. He said: Did I not say that indeed you will never be able to have patience with me? He said: {Do not blame me for what I forgot, and do not be hard upon me in my affair}. So they set out until, when they came upon boys playing on the seashore, among them a boy than whom there was none among the boys more handsome or cleaner, he seized him and killed him. Musa recoiled at that and said: {Have you killed a pure soul for other than a soul? You have certainly done a horrid thing. He said: Did I not tell you that indeed you will never be able to have patience with me?} He said: Embarrassment before his companion seized him, and he felt shy, so he said: {If I ask you about anything after it, then do not keep me in your company; you have received from me an excuse}. So they set out until, when they came to the people of a mean village - and Musa had been afflicted with severe hunger, and they did not show them hospitality - {they found therein a wall about to collapse, so he set it upright}. Musa said to him, because of the hunger that had afflicted them: {If you wished you could have taken for it a payment. He said: This is parting between me and you}; so Musa took hold of the edge of his garment and said: Tell me. He said: As for the ship, it belonged to poor people working at sea, and behind them was a king seizing every ship by force; so when he passed by it and saw it bored, he left it, and its people patched it with a piece of wood and benefited from it. As for the boy, he had been imprinted a disbeliever the day he was imprinted, and love for him had been cast upon his parents; had they disobeyed him in anything, he would have burdened them with transgression and disbelief. So your Lord willed to replace him for them with one better than him in purity and nearer in affection; so his father lay with his mother, and she conceived and bore one better than him in purity and nearer in affection. As for the wall, it belonged to two orphan boys in the city, and beneath it was a treasure for them, up to His saying: That is the interpretation of that over which you could not have patience."
"170","Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Kab, from his father, who said: When a quarter of the night had passed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand and say: O people, remember Allah, remember Allah; the convulsion has come, followed by the succeeding blast; the convulsion has come, followed by the succeeding blast; death has come with what is in it; death has come with what is in it. Ubayy ibn Kab said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, I invoke blessings upon you abundantly; how much of my invocation shall I devote to you? He said: Whatever you wish. He said: A quarter? He said: Whatever you wish, and if you increase it is better. He said: Half? He said: Whatever you wish, and if you increase it is better. He said: Two thirds? He said: Whatever you wish, and if you increase it is better. He said: Shall I devote all my invocation to you? He said: Then your concern will be sufficed and your sin forgiven."
"171","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to me, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr informed, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, I will be the leader of the prophets, their spokesman, and the holder of their intercession, without boast."
"172","Musa ibn Masud narrated to me, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness among people is like that of a man who built a house, perfecting, beautifying, and completing it, and left the place of a brick without laying it; so people go around the building, admiring it and saying: If only the place of this brick were completed. So I am, among the prophets, the place of that brick."
"173","Said ibn Amir narrated to me, from Shubah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdillah ibn Abi Basir, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer one day, then turned to us with his face and said: Is so-and-so present? They said: No. He said: So-and-so? They said: No - for a group of the hypocrites who had not attended the prayer. He said: These two prayers are indeed the heaviest of prayers upon the hypocrites; if they knew what is in them, they would come to them even crawling. Then he said: Adhere to the foremost row, for it is like the row of the angels; if you knew its merit you would hasten to it. He said: Then he said: Your prayer with one man is purer than your prayer alone, and your prayer with two men is purer than your prayer with one man; and the more numerous, the more beloved to Allah, mighty and majestic."
"174","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Thabit, from Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah, from Ubayy ibn Kab: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led the people in prayer and omitted a verse. When he gave salaam he said: Which of you corrected me in my recitation? Ubayy said: I did, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I knew that if anyone corrected me, it would be you."
"175","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, he said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated, he said: A man called Aban informed me, from Ubayy ibn Kab, that he taught a man a surah of the Quran, and he gave him a garment as a gift - or he said: a cloak. He said: He mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If you took it - or he said: If you take it, Muhammad doubted - you would be clothed with a garment of Fire."
"176","Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad informed us, Abu Jafar al-Razi informed, from al-Amash, from Zubayd and Talhah, from Dharr, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High; Say: O disbelievers; and Say: He is Allah, the One."
"177","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated, from Shubah, from Abu Jamrah, he said: Iyas ibn Qatadah narrated, from Qays ibn Ubad, from Ubayy ibn Kab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Be in the row next to me."
"178","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Salil, from Abdillah ibn Rabah al-Ansari, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu al-Mundhir, which verse of the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic, with you is greatest? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Then he said: O Abu al-Mundhir, which verse of the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic, with you is greatest? I said: {Allah, there is no deity but He, the Living, the Sustainer}. He said: He struck my chest and said: May knowledge delight you, O Abu al-Mundhir. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, indeed this verse has a tongue and two lips sanctifying the King at the leg of the Throne."
"179","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated, Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad narrated, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: Two men traced their lineage in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said: I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so; so who are you, may you have no mother? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two men traced their lineage in the time of Musa, peace be upon him. One of them said: I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so, until he counted nine; so who are you, may you have no mother? He said: I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so, son of Islam. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed to Musa: These two who trace lineage - as for you, O claimant to nine in the Fire, you are their tenth in the Fire; and as for you, O claimant to two, you are their third in Paradise."
"180","Ibn Abi Shaybah informed me, he said: I found in the book of my father, Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, he said: I was informed from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Ubayy ibn Kab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Euphrates is about to recede from a mountain of gold; when people hear of it they will hasten to it, and those near it will say: If we leave people to take from it, they will take it all away. So they will fight over it until ninety-nine of every hundred are killed."
"181","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, and Yaqub ibn Ishaq, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Ubayy ibn Kab: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to observe itikaf in the last ten nights of Ramadan; one year he travelled and did not observe itikaf, so in the following year he observed itikaf for twenty nights."
"182","The Musnad of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him. Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated, from Zayd ibn Aslam, Atha ibn Yasar narrated, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Paradise is a hundred degrees; between every two degrees is as between heaven and earth. Al-Firdaws is the highest degree; above it is al-Firdaws, from which burst forth the four rivers of Paradise. So when you ask Allah for Paradise, ask Him for al-Firdaws."
"183","Abu Asim informed us, from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from al-Aswad ibn Thalabah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: I used to teach some of the people of the Suffah, and a bow was gifted to me. I said: It is not wealth; I shall shoot with it in the path of Allah. Then it occurred to me to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish that Allah collar you with it with a collar of Fire, then accept it."
"184","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated, Qatadah informed, from Anas, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the meeting with Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates the meeting with Allah, Allah hates meeting him. Aishah - or one of his wives - said: We indeed hate death. He said: That is not it; rather, the believer, when death comes to him, is given glad tidings of the pleasure of Allah and His honour, so nothing is more beloved to him than what lies before him; so he loves the meeting with Allah, and Allah loves meeting him. As for the disbeliever, when death comes to him, he is given tidings of the punishment of Allah and His retribution, so nothing is more hateful to him than what lies before him; so he hates the meeting with Allah, and Allah hates meeting him."
"185","Ismail ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to me, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim and Abd al-Majid ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to me, from Marwan ibn Salim, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in my nation two men: one of them, Wahb, to whom wisdom is granted; and the other, Ghaylan, whose trial upon this nation is more severe than the trial of Satan. Abu Muhammad said: I heard it from Abd al-Majid."
"186","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Ibn Muhayriz, who said: We were sitting with Ubadah ibn al-Samit when al-Sunabihi came to him weeping. He said to him: What makes you weep? By Allah, if I am martyred I shall certainly testify for you, and if I am granted intercession I shall certainly intercede for you, and if I am able I shall certainly benefit you. I have not concealed from you any hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except a single hadith, and I shall narrate it to you, for I have been encompassed: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, has forbidden the Fire for whoever testifies that none is worthy of worship but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah."
"187","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Zayd ibn Hubab narrated, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, he said: Umayr ibn Hani informed me, he said: I heard Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah say: I heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that Gabriel, peace be upon him, performed ruqyah upon him while he was feverish, saying: In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah upon you, from every ailment harming you, from every envier when he envies, and from every eye; and the name of Allah heals you."
"188","The Musnad of Abu Qatadah ibn Ribi al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed, he said: I was narrated from Abdillah ibn Qatadah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you recite behind me? They said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then do not recite except with the Mother of the Book."
"189","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me having come out to you."
"190","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed, from al-Maqburi, from Abdillah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a funeral to pray over it. He said: Is there a debt upon him? They said: Yes, two dinars. He said: Has he left settlement for them? They said: No. He said: Pray over your companion. Abu Qatadah said: They are upon me, O Messenger of Allah. So he prayed over him."
"191","Said ibn Amir informed us, from Shubah, from Uthman ibn Abdillah ibn Mawhab, from Abdillah, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man to pray over him, and he said: Pray over your companion, for there is a debt upon him. Abu Qatadah said: It is upon me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: With full settlement? He said: With full settlement. The debt upon him was only eighteen or nineteen dirhams."
"192","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah al-Ansari, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon and mentioned jihad, preferring nothing over it except the prescribed prayer. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I am killed in the path of Allah - where am I? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you are killed in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating, then you are in Paradise. He said: And it was revealed to him; when the man turned away he called him and said to him: Except that there be a debt upon him, for he is held by his debt; thus Gabriel, peace be upon him, claimed."
"193","Safwan ibn Isa informed us, from Abdillah ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, he said: A son of Kab ibn Malik narrated to me that he heard Abu Qatadah ibn Ribi say: A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: One at rest and one from whom rest is taken. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what is one at rest and one from whom rest is taken? He said: The believing servant finds rest from the toil of this world and its harm, while from the wicked servant rest is taken by the servants, the lands, the trees, and the beasts."
"194","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Harmalah ibn Iyas al-Shaybani, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about fasting the day of Ashura. He said: It expiates the year. And he was asked about fasting the day of Arafah. He said: It expiates two years: a past year and a coming year."
"195","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Jafar al-Khatmi, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi: that Abu Qatadah had a debt upon a man, and he would come to him seeking repayment, and he would hide from him. One day he came, and a boy came out; he asked him about him, and he said: Yes, he is in the house. So he called to him: O so-and-so, come out, for I have been told you are here. So he came out to him and said: What keeps you away from me? He said: I am in hardship and have nothing. He said: By Allah, are you indeed in hardship? He said: Yes. He said: Then Abu Qatadah wept and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever grants relief to his debtor, or remits it from him, will be in the shade of the Throne on the Day of Resurrection."
"196","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah narrated, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was called for a funeral, he would ask about it; if it was praised with good, he would stand and pray over it, and if it was praised with other than that, he would say to its family: Attend to it yourselves, and would not pray over it."
"197","Abu Nuaym narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile time, for Allah is Time."
"198","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdillah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us in Zuhr prayer, and he would sometimes let us hear a verse; and he would lengthen the first rakah of the dawn prayer and the first rakah of the Zuhr prayer, so we thought he intended thereby that people catch the rakah, meaning the first."
"199","The Musnad of Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him. Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Yahya ibn Jadah, from Abu al-Darda, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wind is from the breath of Allah; when you see it, ask Allah, mighty and majestic, for its good, and seek refuge in Allah from its evil."
"200","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Yuhannas, from Abu al-Darda, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites a hundred verses in a night is not recorded among the heedless; whoever recites two hundred verses is raised among the devout; and whoever recites five hundred to a thousand verses, he wakes with a qintar, the reward of a qirat of which is like the great mound."
"201","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Safwan ibn Abdillah ibn Safwan - and under him was al-Darda - who said: I came to Sham and came to Abu al-Darda but did not meet him; I met Umm al-Darda, and she said: Do you intend Hajj this year? I said: Yes. She said: Then supplicate good for us, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The supplication of the Muslim man is answered for his brother in his absence; at his head is an entrusted angel: whenever he supplicates good for his brother, he says: Amen, and for you the like. He said: Then I went out to the market and met Abu al-Darda, and he said to me the like of that."
"202","Yala narrated, Sufyan narrated, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Habibah, who said: A man bequeathed to me a portion of his wealth to dispose of. So I came to Abu al-Darda and consulted him concerning the poor or the fighters. He said: As for me, had I been in your place I would not have preferred any over the fighters. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The likeness of one who frees a slave at death is like one who gives a gift after satiety."
"203","Abd al-Razzaq informed, Mamar informed, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan used to send to Umm al-Darda, and she would spend the night with his women, and he would ask her about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One night he stood, and called his servant girl, and she was slow upon him, so he cursed her. She said: Do not curse, for Abu al-Darda informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Those who curse frequently will not be intercessors on the Day of Resurrection, nor witnesses."
"204","Wahb ibn Jarir and Abu al-Walid narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Ata al-Kanjarani, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is nothing heavier in the balance than good character."
"205","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Khalid ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi, from Bilal ibn Abi al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your love for a thing blinds and deafens."
"206","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi al-Darda, from his father, who said: A man disparaged a man in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man rebutted him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever defends the honour of his brother will have it as a veil for him from the Fire."
"207","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated, from Qatadah, from Khulayd al-Asari, from Abu al-Darda, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No sun has ever risen except that two angels are dispatched at its sides, calling out - and they make heard all upon the earth except the two weighty beings: O people, hasten to your Lord; for what is little and suffices is better than what is abundant and distracts. And no sun has ever set except that two angels are dispatched at its sides, calling out: O Allah, give the spender a successor, and give the withholder ruin."
"208","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated, from Uthman ibn Hayyan al-Dimashqi, he said: Umm al-Darda informed me, from Abu al-Darda, who said: We saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, on a day intensely hot, until a man would place his hand upon his head from the severity of the heat; and among the people none was fasting except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abdillah ibn Rawahah."
"209","Fihr ibn Awf narrated to me - thus in the printed edition and the manuscript, and the correct is Fahd, with unpointed dal, the لقب of Zayd ibn Awf - Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Bilal ibn Abi al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Neither the green sky has shaded, nor the dusty earth carried, one of more truthful tongue than Abu Dharr."
"210","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shubah narrated, Yazid ibn Khumayr narrated, from Sulayman ibn Marshad, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little, and you would go out crying out, not knowing whether you will be saved or not."
"211","Sulayman ibn Dawud informed us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Jad narrating from Madan ibn Abi Talhah, from Abu al-Darda, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is any one of you unable to recite a third of the Quran in a night? It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who can bear that? He said: He recites: Say: He is Allah, the One."
"212","Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us, Abu Said al-Bakri narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abu al-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun has neither risen nor set upon anyone more excellent or better than Abu Bakr, unless it be a prophet."
"213","Amr ibn Awn narrated to me, Hushaym narrated, from Dawud ibn Amr, from Abdillah ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Khuzai, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You will be called on the Day of Resurrection by your names and the names of your fathers, so make your names good."
"214","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Ibn Uyaynah narrated, from Amr, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Yala ibn Mamlak, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is given his share of gentleness has been given his share of good."
"215","The narration of Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him. Al-Hasan ibn Musa informed us, Ibn Lahiah narrated, Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal narrated that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes to man and says: Who created the heavens? He says: Allah. He says: Who created the earth? He says: Allah - until he says: Then who created Allah? So when any one of you finds that, let him say: I believe in Allah and His Messenger."
"216","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Abu Jafar al-Khatmi, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from his father, that Khuzaymah saw in a dream as though he were prostrating upon the forehead of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed the spirit meets the spirit - or: indeed the spirit meets the spirit, Yazid doubted - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inclined forward, and he commanded him, and he prostrated from behind upon the forehead of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"217","The narration of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Riyah ibn Amr informed, Abu Yahya al-Raqashi narrated, Abu Sawrah, the nephew of Abu Ayyub, narrated to me, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Excellent are those who use toothpicks in ablution and in food."
"218","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Wasil al-Raqashi narrated, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he performed ablution, would rinse his mouth and wipe his beard from beneath with water."
"219","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Wasil al-Raqashi narrated, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would use the tooth-stick at night two or three times; when he stood to pray at night he would pray four rakahs, neither speaking nor commanding anything, and giving salaam between every two rakahs."
"220","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed, from Makhul, he said: Abu Ayyub al-Ansari said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four are among the practices of the messengers: perfuming, marriage, the tooth-stick, and henna."
"221","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed, from Amir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever says: None is worthy of worship but Allah, alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise; in His Hand is good, and He is over all things Powerful - they will be for him like the emancipation of ten necks, or a neck."
"222","Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Rabi ibn Khuthaym, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from a woman of the Ansar, who said: Abu Ayyub - meaning al-Ansari - said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is any one of you unable to recite a third of the Quran in a night? For whoever recites in a night: Allah, the One, the Eternal, has recited a third, or recited a third of the Quran."
"223","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, transmitting it, who said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days; they meet, and this turns away and this turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with salaam."
"224","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, Shubah informed, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from Abu Ayyub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out when the sun had set and said: These are the voices of Jews being punished in their graves."
"225","Abdillah ibn Yazid informed us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, he said: Shurahbil al-Maafiri narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, that he heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning expedition in the path of Allah, or an evening one, is better than what the sun has risen and set upon."
"226","Yala narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Mutattib narrated, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Minjab, from al-Qarthi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: When the sun passed its zenith, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray four rakahs. Abu Ayyub said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer? He said: The gates of heaven are opened when the sun passes its zenith, and they are not closed until Zuhr is prayed; and I love that good should ascend for me therein before the gates of heaven are closed. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is there recitation in all of them? He said: Yes. He said: Is there a separating salaam in them? He said: No, except at their end."
"227","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sufyan ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Asim ibn Sufyan: that they campaigned in the expedition of al-Salasil, and the campaign eluded them, so they remained stationed, then returned to Muawiyah, and with him were Abu Ayyub and Uqbah ibn Amir. Asim said: O Abu Ayyub, we missed the campaign this year, and we have been told that whoever prays in the four mosques, his sin is forgiven. He said: O son of my brother, shall I guide you to what is easier than that? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs ablution as commanded, and prays as commanded, is forgiven for what he has done before. Is it so, O Uqbah? He said: Yes."
"228","Muhadir ibn al-Muwarri narrated to me, Sad ibn Said narrated, from Umar ibn Thabit al-Ansari, who said: I heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts Ramadan, then follows it with six of Shawwal, it is as the fasting of eternity."
"229","Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah, from Abu Ayyub, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate food, he would send me some of what remained, so he sent me a bowl from which he had eaten nothing, and in it was garlic, so I asked him: Is it forbidden? He said: No, but I disliked it because of its smell."
"230","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to me, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from Abu Sirmah, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari that when death came to him, he said: O people, I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which I concealed from you, and were it not for what has come I would not have narrated it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Were it not that you sin, Allah would create a creation who would sin and He would forgive them."
"231","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Zayd ibn Hubab narrated, from Kathir ibn Zayd al-Madani, who said: al-Muttalib ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hantab narrated to me, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: I met Abu Ayyub, and he said: Shall I not command you with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me, to say often: There is no power nor strength except through Allah, for it is from the treasure of Paradise."
"232","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated, from Musa ibn 'Ubaydah, from 'Ubadah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Ubadah ibn 'Awf, who said: Abu Ayyub said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Ayyub, shall I not guide you to a charity beloved to Allah and His Messenger: that you reconcile between people when they hate one another and are corrupted."
"233","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the two verses at the end of Surat al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him."
"234","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Zayd, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sat before him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, as for greeting you with peace, we know it, but what of the prayer upon you, inform us how we send blessings upon you? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent until I wished that the man who asked him had not asked him, then he said: When you send blessings upon me, say: O Allah, bless Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, and bless Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"235","al-Aswad ibn 'Amir informed us, Sharik ibn 'Abdullah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from Abu Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The one consulted is trusted."
"236","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Shu'bah, who said: al-A'mash informed me, who said: I heard Abu Wa'il, from Abu Mas'ud al-Badri, who said: A man among us called Abu Shu'ayb prepared food for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: Come, you and five with you, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you permit me a sixth?"
"237","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from a man, from his father — Sufyan said: I think him 'Iyad ibn 'Iyad — from Abu Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: Indeed among you are hypocrites, so whoever I name, let him stand. So thirty-six stood. Then he said: Indeed among you — or from you — so ask Allah for well-being. Then 'Umar passed by a veiled man whom he knew, and said: What is the matter with you? He informed him of what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said, and he said: Away with you for the rest of the day."
"238","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated, from Mujalid ibn Sa'id, from 'Amir, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised us at the foot of al-'Aqabah on the day of sacrifice, while we were seventy men. 'Uqbah said: I was the youngest of them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: Be brief in speech, for I fear the disbelievers of Quraysh for you. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, ask for yourself, and ask for your Lord, and ask for your companions, and inform us what the reward from Allah and from you is? He said: I ask you for my Lord that you believe in Allah and associate nothing with Him, and I ask you to obey me so I may guide you to the path of right guidance, and I ask you for myself and my companions that you share with us from what you possess and protect us as you protect yourselves. If you do that, for you from Allah is Paradise, and from me. He said: So we extended our hands and pledged allegiance to him."
"239","Ibrahim ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to me, al-Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, who said: While I was beating a slave boy of mine with a whip of mine, I heard a voice behind me: Know, O Abu Mas'ud. I did not turn nor comprehend out of anger until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew near me, so I turned, and when I saw him the whip fell from my hand out of awe of him, or I threw it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Know, O Abu Mas'ud, that Allah Almighty has more power over you than you have over him. He said: I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never beat a slave boy of mine after this."
"240","Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Sharik narrated, from al-Rukayn, from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I leave among you that which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my progeny, my household. For they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond."
"241","al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: When this verse was revealed: Not equal are those who sit among the believers and those who strive in the path of Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a shoulder blade and wrote it. Then 'Abdullah ibn Umm Maktum came and complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Allah Almighty revealed: Not equal are those who sit among the believers, other than those with disability."
"242","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Shu'bah narrated, from 'Adi ibn Thabit, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Thabit say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Uhud, some people turned back on the way. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were divided into two groups concerning them: one group saying, we will kill them, and one group saying, we will not kill them. So Allah Almighty revealed: What is the matter with you that you are two groups concerning the hypocrites, while Allah has cast them back for what they earned. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed it is Taybah; it expels impurity as fire expels the dross of silver."
"243","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated, from al-A'mash, from Thabit ibn 'Ubayd, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I write to a people, and I fear they may add to or omit from me, so learn Syriac. So I learned it in seventeen days."
"244","'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr and 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Zayd ibn Thabit that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah fight the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"245","Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Kathir ibn Aflah, from Zayd ibn Thabit: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to glorify Allah thirty-three times at the end of every prayer, and praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times. He said: Then a man saw in a dream that a man said to him: If only you made them twenty-five and added the tahlil to them. He said: So he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Then do so."
"246","'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, that Zayd ibn Thabit said: When we wrote the codices, I missed a verse I used to hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I found it with Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Ansari: Among the believers are men true to what they promised Allah, up to: alteration. He said: Khuzaymah was called the one of two testimonies; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made his testimony equal to that of two men, and he was killed on the day of Siffin with 'Ali, may Allah have mercy on him."
"247","'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, Abu Sinan informed me, from Wahb ibn Khalid al-Himsi, from Ibn al-Daylami, who said: Something concerning the decree entered my mind, so I came to Ubayy ibn Ka'b and asked him. He said: Indeed Allah Almighty, if He punished the inhabitants of His heavens and His earth, He would not wrong them, and if He had mercy on them, His mercy would be better for them than their deeds. If you spent Uhud — or he said: like Uhud — in gold, Allah would not accept it until you believe in the decree and know that what struck you was never to miss you, and what missed you was never to strike you. If you died upon other than this, you would die upon other than the fitrah upon which Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was created. He said: So I left him and came to Ibn Mas'ud and asked him, and he said to me the same. He said: Then I came to Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman and asked him, and he said to me the same. Then I came to Zayd ibn Thabit and asked him, and he narrated to me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"248","'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: We took the pre-dawn meal with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we went out to prayer. He said: I said: How much was between them? He said: As much as a man recites fifty verses."
"249","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir narrated, from Abu al-Zinad, from Sa'd ibn Sulayman, from Zayd ibn Thabit: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? Say often: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"250","'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated, Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu al-Nadr narrating from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zayd ibn Thabit: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a chamber in the mosque made of mats, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in it for some nights until people gathered to him. Then one night they missed his voice and thought he had slept, so some of them began clearing their throats for him to come out to them. He said: That which I saw of your doing continued until I feared it would be made obligatory upon you, and if it were made obligatory you could not uphold it. So pray, O people, in your houses, for the best prayer of a man is in his house except the obligatory prayer."
"251","'Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Yazid ibn Qusayt, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I recited al-Najm before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not prostrate in it."
"252","Muhammad ibn 'Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Salit ibn Yasar ibn Salit ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated, from Maryam bint Sa'd ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from Umm Sa'd bint Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' — who was the mother of Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit — from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever keeps a horse in the path of Allah, it will be his shield from the Fire."
"253","Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated, Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj narrated, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from mukhabarah. I said: What is mukhabarah? He said: That you take land for a half, a third, or a quarter."
"254","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to us, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a garden of Banu al-Najjar upon a mule of his, and we were with him, it swerved with him and almost threw him, and there were six or five or four graves. He said: Who knows the people of these graves? A man said: I do. He said: When did they die? He said: They died in polytheism. He said: This nation will be tested in their graves. Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have supplicated Allah to let you hear from the punishment of the grave what I hear. Then he turned to us with his face and said: Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Fire. We said: We seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Fire. He said: Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave. We said: We seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave. He said: Seek refuge with Allah from tribulations, what is apparent of them and what is hidden. We said: We seek refuge with Allah from tribulations, what is apparent of them and what is hidden. He said: Seek refuge with Allah from the tribulation of the Dajjal. We said: We seek refuge with Allah from the tribulation of the Dajjal."
"255","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Waki' narrated, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Zayd ibn Thabit that he was asked about recitation in Zhuhr and 'Asr, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would prolong the standing and move his lips."
"256","'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Nibras narrated, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, from Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The prayer was established, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out walking, and I was with him, and he shortened his steps. Then he said to me: Do you know why I did this? So that our steps in seeking prayer may be many."
"257","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, al-'Ala ibn Salih narrated, Abu Sulayman narrated: He prayed with Zayd ibn Arqam over a funeral and magnified Allah five times over it, so I said: Was it forgetfulness or deliberate? He said: No, rather deliberate; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray it so."
"258","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Husam ibn al-Misakk narrated, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim ibn 'Awf al-Shaybani, Zayd ibn Arqam narrated: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them in the mosque of Quba and saw them praying Duha, and said: This is the prayer of the oft-returning. He said: And they used to pray it when the young camels felt the heat."
"259","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sallam ibn Miskin Abu 'Abdullah al-Basri informed us, from 'Aidhullah al-Mujashi'i, from Abu Dawud, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We said — or they said, Yazid doubted — O Messenger of Allah, what are these sacrifices? He said: The practice of your father Ibrahim. They said: What is in them for us? He said: For every hair, a good deed. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, then wool? He said: For every hair of wool, a good deed."
"260","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from al-Harith ibn Shubayl, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: One of us would speak to his companion in prayer about a need, until was revealed: Guard the prayers and the middle prayer, and stand for Allah devoutly. So we were commanded to be silent."
"261","'Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I asked him: How many expeditions did you take part in with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Seventeen expeditions. I said: How many expeditions did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take part in? He said: Nineteen expeditions."
"262","'Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: I was with my uncle and heard 'Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul saying to his companions: Do not spend upon those with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse, and if we return to Madinah the mightier will surely expel the lowlier from it. I mentioned that to my uncle, and he mentioned it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and I informed him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for 'Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul and his companions, and they swore they had not said it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disbelieved me and believed him. A grief befell me the like of which never befell me, and I sat in the house. My uncle said to me: You intended only that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disbelieved you and despised you?! Then Allah Almighty revealed: When the hypocrites come to you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me and recited it, then said: Indeed Allah Almighty has confirmed you."
"263","Ya'la narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated, from Thumamah ibn 'Uqbah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: A man from the People of the Book came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu al-Qasim, you claim the people of Paradise eat and drink. He said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, a man among them will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, intercourse, and desire. He said: Then one who eats and drinks will need to relieve himself?! He said: Sweat pouring like the scent of musk; when that happens his belly shrinks."
"264","Ya'la and Muhammad, sons of 'Ubayd, narrated to us, both saying: Yusuf ibn Suhayb narrated, from Habib ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not trim his mustache is not from us."
"265","Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us, Abu Hayyan al-Taymi informed us, from Yazid ibn Hayyan, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, O people, I am only a human; the messenger of my Lord is about to come to me and I will answer him. I leave among you the two weighty things: the first is the Book of Allah, in it is guidance and light, so hold fast to the Book of Allah and take it. He urged upon the Book of Allah and encouraged it, then said: And my household; I remind you of Allah concerning my household, three times. Husayn said: O Zayd, who are his household? Are not his wives from his household? He said: Yes, his wives are from his household, but his household are those forbidden charity after him. He said: Who are they? He said: The family of 'Ali, the family of Ja'far, the family of 'Aqil, and the family of al-'Abbas. He said: Were all of these forbidden charity? He said: Yes."
"266","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Shu'bah narrated, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Abu Hamzah, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam say: He was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You are not but one part of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond. I said: How many were you then? He said: Seven hundred men or eight hundred men."
"267","Muhadir ibn al-Muwarri' narrated to me, 'Asim ibn Sulayman narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We said: Teach us — or narrate to us. He said: I will teach you only what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from inability and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, old age and the punishment of the grave. O Allah, grant our souls their piety, and You are the best to purify them; You are their Guardian and Master. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from a heart that does not humble itself, a soul that is not satisfied, knowledge that does not benefit, and a supplication that is not answered."
"268","Sulayman ibn Dawud informed us, from Shu'bah, from Abu 'Abdullah al-Shami, who said: I heard Mu'awiyah delivering a sermon, saying: O people of Sham, al-Ansari narrated to us — Shu'bah said: meaning Zayd ibn Arqam — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will always be a group of my nation upon the truth until the command of Allah comes, and I see them to be you, O people of Sham."
"269","'Affan ibn Muslim and Abu al-Walid narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah that Ibn 'Abbas said to Zayd ibn Arqam: Did you not know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given a limb of game while in ihram and did not accept it? He said: Yes."
"270","'Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Sufyan, from Jabir, from Khaythamah, from Zayd ibn Arqam: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him while he complained of his eyes, and said: What if your eyes were as they are — or something like this — what would you do? He said: Then I would be patient and seek reward. He said: If your eyes were as they are, you would meet Allah without sin."
"271","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated, from al-A'mash, from Yazid ibn Hayyan, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: A man from the Jews cast a spell upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He fell ill, and Jibril came to him and sent down upon him the two Mu'awwidhatayn, and said: A man from the Jews has cast a spell upon you, and the spell is in the well of so-and-so. He said: So he sent 'Ali, who brought it. He said: So he commanded him to undo the knots and recite a verse. He kept reciting and untying until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as though released from bonds. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not mention to that Jew anything of what he had done to him, nor did I see it in his face."
"272","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated, that Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban informed him that Abu 'Amrah, freedman of Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, informed him that he heard Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani narrating that a man from the Muslims died in Khaybar, and they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him to pray over him. He said: Pray over your companion. The faces of the people changed, and when he saw what troubled them, he said: Your companion misappropriated from the spoils in the path of Allah. He said: So we searched his belongings and found beads from the beads of the Jews, by Allah not worth two dirhams."
"273","Abu 'Ali al-Hanafi informed me, Malik ibn Anas narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, that his father informed him that 'Abdullah ibn Qays ibn Makhramah informed him that Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani said: I said: I will observe the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tonight. So I rested my head on his threshold or his tent. He stood and prayed two light rak'ahs, then prayed two long rak'ahs, long, long, then stood and prayed two rak'ahs less than them, then prayed two rak'ahs less than those before them, then prayed two rak'ahs less than those before them, then prayed two rak'ahs less than those before them, then prayed witr. That was thirteen rak'ahs."
"274","'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Sufyan narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Labid, from al-Muttalib ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Khallad ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril came to me and said to me: Command your companions to raise their voices with the talbiyah, for it is from the rites of Hajj."
"275","Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated, from 'Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take your houses as graves; pray in them."
"276","Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated, from 'Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever provides iftar for a fasting person, there is written for him the like of his reward, except that it does not diminish anything from the reward of the fasting person. And whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah or looks after his family, there is written for him the like of his reward, except that it does not diminish anything from the reward of the warrior."
"277","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Shayban narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has raided, and whoever looks after a warrior among his family with good has raided."
"278","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Majishun informed us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the rooster, for it calls to prayer."
"279","Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid, freedman of al-Munba'ith, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about lost property. He said: Know its container and its tie, then announce it for a year. If its seeker comes, otherwise do with it as you wish. He said: Then the stray sheep? He said: It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf. He said: Then the stray camel? He said: What have you to do with it? It has its water skin and its sandals; it comes to water and eats trees until its master finds it."
"280","'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr informed us, who said: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from 'Ata ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then prays two rak'ahs without heedlessness in them, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"281","Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to me, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, who said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would leave for the market, and if an arrow were shot I could see where it landed."
"282","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from Salim, from Busr ibn Sa'id, who said: Abu Juhaym, son of the sister of Ubayy ibn Ka'b, sent me: Ask Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani what you heard concerning one who passes in front of the praying person? He mentioned from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: That he stand forty is better for him than to pass in front of him. I do not know whether he said forty years, or months, or days, or hours."
"283","al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated, 'Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father Zayd ibn Harithah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That Jibril, peace be upon him, in the first of what was revealed to him, showed him ablution and prayer. When he finished ablution, he took a handful of water and sprinkled his private part with it."
"284","'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, Humayd ibn Hani narrated to me, who said: 'Amr ibn Hurayth informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever you lighten of the work of your servant is a reward for you in your scales."
"285","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated, from al-Suddi, who said: One who heard 'Amr ibn Hurayth informed me, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in patched sandals."
"286","Abu 'Asim informed us, Sa'id ibn Zayd informed us, from 'Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Abu al-Hasan al-Himsi, from 'Amr ibn Murrah — who had companionship — that he said to Mu'awiyah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any ruler or judge — 'Ali doubted — who closes his door to those of need, poverty, and misery, Allah will close His door to his need, poverty, and misery."
"287","Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Bajali narrated to us, Qays Abu 'Umarah narrated to me, who said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm narrating from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who consoles his Muslim brother for his calamity except that Allah Almighty will clothe him from the robes of honor on the Day of Resurrection."
"288","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, Qays Abu 'Umarah narrated to me, who said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm narrating from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever visits a sick person continues wading in mercy until when he sits he is immersed in it, then when he returns he continues wading in it until he returns to where he came from."
"289","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to me, from Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf al-Muzani, who said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a practice of mine that has died, and it is acted upon, he has the reward of whoever among people acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever innovates an innovation and it is acted upon, upon him is the burden of whoever among people acts upon it, without diminishing anything from their burdens."
"290","Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, who said: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to magnify Allah seven times in the first rak'ah of the two Eids, and five times in the last rak'ah."
"291","Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Bajali narrated to me, who said: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In Friday there is an hour of the day in which the servant does not ask for anything except that he is given what he asks. It was said: Which hour is it? He said: From when the prayer is established until finishing from it."
"292","Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la, from his father, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, from his father that two disputants came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to 'Amr: Judge between them. I said: You are more entitled to that than I. He said: Even so. He said: I do not judge. He said: If you are right, ten good deeds are written for you, and if you strive and err, one good deed is written for you."
"293","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi narrated, who said: I heard my father say: I heard Abu Qays, freedman of 'Amr ibn al-'As, say: I heard 'Amr ibn al-'As say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The difference between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the pre-dawn meal."
"294","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, from Abu Ja'far al-Khatmi, from 'Umarah ibn Khuzaymah, who said: We were with 'Amr ibn al-'As on a Hajj or 'Umrah, and when we were at Marr al-Zahran, there was a woman in her howdah placing her hand on her howdah. When he alighted, he entered the ravine and we entered with him. He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this place, when there were many crows, and there was a white-bellied crow with red beak and legs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of the women will enter Paradise except like this crow among these crows."
"295","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to me, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated, from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, from 'Amr ibn al-'As, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed me over the army of Dhat al-Salasil. I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is most beloved to you? He said: 'A'ishah. I said: Among men? He said: Her father then. He said: I said: Then whom? He said: Then 'Umar. He said: Then he listed men."
"296","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us, my father narrated to me, 'Abdullah ibn 'Isa ibn Buhayr narrated, who said: My father narrated to me: He was in the mosque when 'Amr ibn al-'As was sitting, and he said to me: Are you from the people of Yemen? I said: Yes. He said to me: Come near me, I will narrate to you a hadith by which your eyes will be delighted. He said: So I drew near him, and 'Amr said: While we were one day sitting, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and sat with us, then said: Where are my brothers of whom I am and who are of me; I will enter Paradise and they will enter with me. Then he stood and left, and it was not long before he returned and sat, then said: Where are my brothers of whom I am and who are of me; I will enter Paradise and they will enter with me. Then he stood and left. Some of us said to others: If only we asked: Are others than us they, O Messenger of Allah? It was only a little before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and sat, and said: Where are my brothers of whom I am and who are of me; I will enter Paradise and they will enter with me. We said: O Messenger of Allah, are others than us they? He said: Yes, they are the people of Yemen, cast aside in the outskirts of the earth, turned away from the doors of rulers; one of them dies with his need in his chest, never fulfilled."
"297","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hariz ibn 'Uthman informed us, Salim ibn 'Amir narrated, from 'Amr ibn 'Abasah, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at 'Ukaz, and said: Who has followed you in this matter? He said: A free man and a slave — and with him were only Abu Bakr and Bilal. He said: Go until Allah enables His Messenger, then come to him after. He said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom, something you know and I do not, which benefits me and does not harm you: what hour is closest to Allah, and what hour is to be avoided? He said: O 'Amr ibn 'Abasah, you have asked me about something no one before you asked me about. The Lord, Blessed and Exalted, descends in the last part of the night and forgives, except for polytheism and oppression. Prayer is prescribed and witnessed until the sun rises, for it rises upon the horn of Satan, and it is the prayer of the disbelievers. So refrain from prayer until the sun rises high. When it is high, prayer is witnessed until midday. When midday is level, refrain from prayer, for at that time Hell is stoked. When the shadow inclines, prayer is witnessed until it declines toward sunset, for it sets upon the horn of Satan and it is the prayer of the disbelievers. So refrain from prayer until the sun has set."
"298","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Bishr ibn Numayr informed us, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, from 'Amr ibn 'Abasah that Shurahbil ibn Hasanah asked him: O 'Amr, is there a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there is no forgetfulness nor addition? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs ablution and washes his hands, his sins exit from his fingertips. When he rinses his mouth and nose, his sins exit from his ears. When he washes his face, his sins exit from his face. When he washes his hands, his sins exit from his hands. When he wipes his head, his sins exit from the ends of his hair. When he washes his feet, his sins exit from his toes. If he sits upon his ablution, he has its reward, and if he stands devoting himself to his prayer, he leaves as his mother bore him, free of sins. Shurahbil said to him: O 'Amr, look at what you say? He said: If I had heard it only once or twice or thrice, I would not narrate it to you. And he said: Whoever grows a white hair in the path of Allah, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever shoots the enemy with an arrow that reaches — whether it hits or misses — it equals freeing a slave."
"299","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hariz ibn 'Uthman informed us, Salim ibn 'Amir narrated that 'Amr ibn 'Abasah was with Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, and he said: O 'Amr, is there a hadith you narrate to us from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there is no deficiency nor forgetfulness? He said: Yes, by the One in whose Hand is the soul of 'Amr: There is no man who grows a white hair in the path of Allah except that Allah makes it light on the Day of Resurrection. There is no man who shoots an arrow at the enemy in the path of Allah Almighty, missing or hitting, except that it is for him like freeing a slave from the children of Isma'il. No one frees a believing slave except that every limb of it ransoms a limb of him from the Fire. He said: O 'Amr ibn 'Abasah, you narrate a tremendous hadith. 'Amr said: Wretched is what I have; my age is advanced and my bones are thin, and I have no motive to lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard it from him more than once."
"300","Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Dinar narrated, from Muhammad ibn Dhakwan, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from 'Amr ibn 'Abasah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, who has followed you in this matter? He said: A free man and a slave. I said: What is Islam? He said: Good speech and feeding food. I said: What is faith? He said: Patience and generosity. I said: Which Islam is best? He said: One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. I said: Which faith is best? He said: Good character. I said: Which prayer is best? He said: Lengthy standing. I said: Which migration is best? He said: That you abandon what your Lord dislikes. I said: Which jihad is best? He said: One whose horse is hamstrung and his blood shed. I said: Which hour is best? He said: The last depth of the night. Then prayer is prescribed and witnessed until dawn appears. When dawn appears, there is no prayer except two rak'ahs until you pray Fajr. When you pray Fajr, refrain from prayer until the sun rises. When the sun rises, refrain from prayer, for it rises in the horn of Satan, and the disbelievers pray to it. Refrain until it rises high. When it is high, prayer is prescribed and witnessed until the shadow stands like a spear. When it is so, there is no prayer until the sun declines. When it declines, prayer is prescribed and witnessed until the sun sets. When it is near sunset, refrain from prayer, for it sets — or disappears — in the horn of Satan, and the disbelievers pray to it."
"301","'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from 'Amr ibn 'Abasah, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam? He said: That you submit your heart to Allah Almighty, and that the Muslims be safe from your tongue and hand. He said: Which Islam is best? He said: Faith. He said: What is faith? He said: That you believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and resurrection after death. He said: Which faith is best? He said: Migration. He said: What is migration? He said: That you abandon evil. He said: Which migration is best? He said: Jihad. He said: What is jihad? He said: That you fight the disbelievers when you meet them. He said: Which jihad is best? He said: One whose horse is hamstrung and his blood shed. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then two deeds are the best deeds except for one who does their like: an accepted Hajj, or an 'Umrah."
"302","'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from 'Amr ibn 'Abasah that he was sitting with his companions when a man said: Who will narrate to us a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? 'Amr said: I will. He said: It is for Allah, your father — and beware. He said: I heard him say: Whoever grows a white hair in the path of Allah, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: It is for Allah, your father — and beware. He said: I heard him say: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, that equals freeing a slave. He said: It is for Allah, your father — and beware. He said: And I heard him say: Whoever frees a soul, Allah frees with every limb of it a limb of him from the Fire. He said: And I heard him say: Whoever frees two souls, Allah frees with every two limbs of them a limb of him from the Fire. He said: It is for Allah, your father — and beware. He said: And a hadith: had I not heard it from him except once or twice or thrice or four or five times, I would not have narrated it to you. He said: I heard him say: There is no Muslim servant who performs ablution and washes his face except that the sins of his face fall from the ends of his beard. When he washes his hands, the sins of his hands fall from between his fingers and nails. When he wipes his head, the sins of his head fall from the ends of his hair. When he washes his feet, the sins of his feet fall from their soles. If he comes to a congregational mosque and prays in it, his reward falls upon Allah Almighty. If he stands and prays two rak'ahs, they are expiation for him."
"303","Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated, from Makhul, from 'Amr ibn 'Abasah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah is distanced from the Fire by a journey of a hundred years."
"304","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated, Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated, Abu Zabyah informed me that Shurahbil ibn al-Simt called 'Amr ibn 'Abasah al-Sulami and said: O Ibn 'Abasah, will you narrate to me a hadith you heard yourself from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there is no addition nor lie, and do not narrate to me from another who heard it from him besides you? He said: Yes, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My love is assured for those who love one another for My sake, and My love is assured for those who spend for one another for My sake, and My love is assured for those who support one another for My sake, and My love is assured for those who are just to one another for My sake, and My love is assured for those who visit one another for My sake. 'Amr ibn 'Abasah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any Muslim man who shoots an arrow in the path of Allah that reaches — missing or hitting — he has reward like a slave he freed from the children of Isma'il. Any man who grows a white hair in Islam, it is light for him. Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, every limb of the freed ransoms a limb of the freer from the Fire. Any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, every limb of the freed ransoms a limb of the freer from the Fire. Any Muslim man — or woman — for whom Allah takes in advance from his loins three who did not reach puberty, they are a shield for him from the Fire. Any man who rises to ablution intending prayer and completes the ablution to its places is safe from every sin or fault of his. If he stands for prayer, Allah raises him a degree by it, and if he sits, he sits sound. Shurahbil ibn al-Simt said: Did you hear this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), O Ibn 'Abasah? He said: Yes, by the One besides whom there is no god, had I not heard this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than once or twice or thrice or four or five or six or seven times — he stopped at seven — I would not have sworn to narrate it to anyone among people, but by Allah I do not know the number of times I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"305","al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, 'Abd al-Malik Abu Ja'far informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Sa'd ibn al-Atwal, that his brother died leaving three hundred dirhams and dependents. He said: I wanted to spend it upon his dependents, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother is held back by his debt, so settle it for him. He said: So he settled it for him, then said: O Messenger of Allah, I have settled except a woman who claimed two dinars and has no proof. He said: Give her, for she is truthful."
"306","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Isa, from a man, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no commander of ten who meets Allah Almighty except bound; nothing releases him except justice. And there is no man who recites the Quran then forgets it except that he meets Allah maimed."
"307","Husayn al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Isa ibn Fa'id, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever recites the Quran then forgets it will come to Allah on the Day of Resurrection leprous, and whoever is put in charge of ten will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bound; nothing frees him from his bonds except justice."
"308","Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, who said: My father narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn 'Amr ibn Shurahbil ibn Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah al-Ansari, from his father, from his grandfather: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged by oath with a witness in claims of rights."
"309","Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to me, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from 'Amr ibn Shurahbil ibn Sa'id, from his father, from his grandfather, from Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah that a man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Inform us about Friday, what good is in it? He said: In it are five qualities: in it Allah created Adam, and in it He sent him down, and in it Allah took the soul of Adam, and in it is an hour in which the servant does not ask Allah for anything except that Allah gives it to him, so long as he does not ask for sin or severing kinship, and in it the Hour will come. There is no close angel, nor heaven, nor earth, nor mountains, nor wind, except that they fear Friday."
"310","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Bukayr ibn 'Ata that he heard 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'mar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hajj is 'Arafat — or 'Arafah — and whoever catches the night of Muzdalifah before dawn breaks, his Hajj is complete. The days of Mina are three, and whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him."
"311","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Sakan ibn al-Mughirah Abu Muhammad, freedman of the family of 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, who said: al-Walid ibn Ziyad narrated to me, from Farqad Abu Talhah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Khabbab al-Sulami, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon, and he urged upon the army of hardship. 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, one hundred camels with their saddles and packs in the path of Allah Almighty. Then he urged a second time, and 'Uthman ibn 'Affan stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, two hundred camels with their saddles and packs in the path of Allah Almighty. Then he urged a third time, and 'Uthman ibn 'Affan stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, three hundred camels with their saddles and packs in the path of Allah Almighty. 'Abd al-Rahman said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as he descended from the pulpit saying: Whatever 'Uthman does after this will not harm him; whatever 'Uthman does after this will not harm him."
"312","Muhammad ibn Bishr al-'Abdi Abu 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from 'Azrah, from Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with: Glorify the name of your Lord, Most High, and: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One. When he gave salam, he would say three times: Glory be to the Sovereign, the Most Holy."
"313","'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr narrated to us, who said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from Sa'id ibn Khalid, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Uthman al-Taymi: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing the frog."
"314","'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, who said: Ma'mar narrated, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Zayd ibn Sallam, from his grandfather, who said: Mu'awiyah wrote to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl: Teach the people what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he gathered them and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Learn the Quran, and when you learn it, do not go to excess in it, nor turn away from it, nor eat by it, nor seek increase by it. Then he said: The merchants are the wicked. They said: O Messenger of Allah, has not Allah permitted trade and forbidden usury? He said: Yes, but they swear and sin. Then he said: The corrupt are the people of the Fire. They said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the corrupt? He said: Women. They said: O Messenger of Allah, are they not our mothers and sisters? He said: Yes, but when they are given they are not grateful, and when they are tried they are not patient. He said: Then he said: Let the rider greet the walker, and the walker the seated, and the fewer the more. Whoever answers the salam has it, and whoever does not answer, there is nothing against him."
"315","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Ibn 'Awn informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you see the funeral, stand — or he said: halt — until it passes you. He said: Ibn 'Umar, when he saw a funeral, would stand until it passed him. He said: And when Ibn 'Umar went out with a funeral, he would turn his back to the graves."
"316","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sa'd ibn Sa'id informed us, 'Asim ibn 'Ubaydullah narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on an expedition on a dark black night and did not know the qiblah, so each man among us made a mosque of stones before him, then we prayed. In the morning we were toward other than the qiblah, so we mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: To Allah belong the east and the west; wherever you turn, there is the Face of Allah."
"317","Zayd ibn al-Hubab al-'Ukli informed us, Shu'bah narrated, from 'Asim ibn 'Ubaydullah al-'Umari, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the pulpit: There is no servant who sends blessings upon me except that the angels send blessings upon him so long as he sends blessings upon me, so let him do little of that or much."
"318","'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from 'Asim ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Asim, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) using the siwak while fasting, more times than I can count."
"319","'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah informed me, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying the voluntary prayer upon his mount in every direction."
"320","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hariz ibn 'Uthman informed us, Habban ibn Zayd narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said while upon the pulpit: Show mercy and you will be shown mercy; forgive and Allah will forgive you. Woe to the funnels of speech, and woe to the persistent who persist upon what they did while they know."
"321","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from 'Ata, from Ibn 'Amr, and from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-'Abbas, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: It has reached me that you fast the day and stand the night. I said: I do that, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do not do it, for if you do that the eyes sink and the soul wearies. Your family has a right upon you, your self has a right upon you, and your body has a right upon you. Rather fast three days of every month, for they are the fast of the lifetime. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am stronger than that. He said: He who fasts the lifetime has not fasted, but if you must do, then fast the fast of Dawud, for he would fast a day and break a day, and would not flee when he met the enemy."
"322","'Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from 'Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Four, whoever has them in him is a pure hypocrite, and whoever has a trait of them in him has a trait of hypocrisy until he leaves it: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks, when he disputes he acts wickedly, and when he covenants he betrays."
"323","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, Mu'awiyah ibn Sa'id al-Tujibi narrated, who said: I heard Abu Qabil al-Misri say: I heard 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies on Friday or the night of Friday is protected from the trial of the grave."
"324","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Salim, from Jabban, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The one who reminds of favors, the habitual drinker of wine, and the child of adultery will not enter Paradise."
"325","'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among the gravest of sins is that a man revile his parents. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he revile his parents? He said: He exchanges insults with a man, so he reviles his father, then the other reviles his father; then he reviles his mother, then the other reviles his mother."
"326","Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us, Abu Hayyan al-Taymi informed us, from Abu Zur'ah ibn 'Amr ibn Jarir, who said: Three men sat with Marwan in Madinah and heard him narrating that the first of the signs to emerge is the Dajjal. The group stood from Marwan and sat with 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr and informed him of what Marwan said. 'Abdullah said: Marwan said nothing. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first of the signs to emerge is the rising of the sun from its west, and the Beast. Whichever of them is before the other, the other follows it closely. Then he began narrating: When the sun sets, it comes beneath the Throne, prostrates, and seeks permission to return, and it is permitted. When Allah Almighty wills it to rise from its west, it comes beneath the Throne, prostrates, and seeks permission to return, and nothing is answered to it. He said: Then it returns seeking permission to return, and nothing is answered to it. He said: And it knew, had it been permitted, it would not reach the east. It says: My Lord, how far is the east, and who is there for people? He said: Until when the night is like a collar, it comes beneath the Throne and seeks permission. It is said to it: Rise from your place. He said: 'Abdullah used to read the books. He said: So he recited: The day when some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good in its faith."
"327","Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is enjoyment, and the best of its enjoyment is the righteous woman. And there is no supplication answered faster than the supplication of one absent for another absent."
"328","Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad al-Ifriqi narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not marry women for their beauty, for perhaps their beauty will destroy them, nor marry them for their wealth, for perhaps their wealth will make them transgress. Marry them for religion; a black slave woman with pierced nose, of religion, is better."
"329","Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, al-Ifriqi narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever suffers a headache in the path of Allah then seeks reward, Allah Almighty forgives him what preceded of sin."
"330","Ya'la narrated to us, al-Ifriqi narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask Allah for well-being. When you meet them, be firm and remember Allah Almighty much. If they shout and clamor, upon you is silence."
"331","Ya'la narrated to us, al-Ifriqi narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fastest supplication to be answered is the supplication of one absent for another absent."
"332","Ya'la narrated to us, al-Ifriqi narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves a man and says: I love you for Allah Almighty, and both enter Paradise, and he is of higher degree than him, he is joined to him."
"333","Ya'la narrated to us, al-Ifriqi narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer after Fajr except two rak'ahs."
"334","Ya'la narrated to us, al-Ifriqi narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whom do you count as martyr? They said: One killed in the path of Allah. He said: Then the martyrs of my nation are few. One killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, one who drowns in the path of Allah is a martyr, and one killed by plague is a martyr."
"335","Ya'la narrated to us, al-Ifriqi narrated, from a man, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is reconciling relations."
"336","'Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um al-Ifriqi narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the Muslim? He said: One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. He said: Who is the believer? He said: One whom people trust with their wealth and selves. He said: Who is the emigrant? He said: One who abandons evil deeds. He said: Who is the mujahid? He said: One who strives against his soul for Allah Almighty."
"337","'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Six gatherings: a Muslim is in none of them except that he is guaranteed by Allah Almighty: in the path of Allah, or in a congregational mosque, or with a sick person, or following a funeral, or in his house, or with a just ruler whom he supports and honors for Allah Almighty."
"338","'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: We were sitting with him, and he said: Shall I not teach you words which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach, which he would say when he wished to sleep? I said: Yes. So he brought out a sheet for us, and in it was: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, You are the Lord of all things and their Sovereign. I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, without partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and messenger, and the angels bear witness. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from Satan and his association, and I seek refuge with You from committing evil against myself or bringing it upon a Muslim."
"339","'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated, from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, then the Scale will be brought, then ninety-nine scrolls will be brought, each scroll of them as far as the eye can see, containing his faults and sins, and placed in one pan of the Scale. Then there will be brought out for him a sheet like this — and he held his thumb upon half his finger — the supplication in it is the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and messenger — and placed in the other pan, and it outweighs his faults and sins."
"340","'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, Rabi'ah ibn Sayf al-Ma'afiri narrated to me, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A disbeliever's funeral passes by us, shall we stand for it? He said: Yes, stand for it, for you do not stand for it; you stand only in reverence for the One who takes souls."
"341","'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated, Shurahbil ibn Sharik narrated, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Successful is one who submits, is given sufficiency, and Allah contents him with what He gave him."
"342","'Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated, from Shurahbil ibn Sharik, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best of companions with Allah is the best of them to his companion, and the best of neighbors with Allah is the best of them to his neighbor."
"343","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh and Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu Hani al-Khawlani, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, that he heard Abdallah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah decreed the decreed measures fifty thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth."
"344","Ya'mar ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abdallah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, saying: Huayy ibn Abdallah narrated to me, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdallah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you visits a sick person, let him say: O Allah, heal Your servant, that he may wound an enemy for You or walk to prayer for You."
"345","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Abdallah ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdallah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever keeps silent is saved."
"346","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, saying: Abdallah ibn Junadah al-Ma'afiri narrated to me, that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli narrated to him, from Abdallah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The world is the prison of the believer; when he leaves the world, he leaves the prison."
"347","Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Bakr ibn Amr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdallah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The gift for the believer is death."
"348","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Abu Hani al-Khawlani narrated to me, saying: I heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli say: I heard Abdallah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The hearts of the children of Adam, all of them, are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful, blessed and exalted is He, as a single heart; He turns it as He wills. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, Turner of hearts, turn our hearts to Your obedience."
"349","Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, al-Ifriqi narrated to us, from Imran ibn Abdallah, from Abdallah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three matters: whoever takes on debt for them, then dies without repaying, Allah, mighty and majestic is He, will repay on his behalf: a man who is in the path of Allah and whose strength weakens, so he strengthens himself with a debt against the enemy, then dies without repaying; a man with whom a Muslim dies and who finds nothing with which to shroud him nor anything with which to bury him except through a debt, then dies without repaying; and a man who fears temptation for himself and so preserves his chastity by marrying a woman through a debt, then dies without repaying; Allah, mighty and majestic is He, will repay on their behalf on the Day of Resurrection."
"350","Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, al-Ifriqi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi', from Abdallah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The land of the non-Arabs will be opened to you, and you will find therein houses called baths; men shall not enter them except with a waist-wrapper, and keep women from entering them except one who is sick or in postnatal bleeding."
"351","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Hudayj ibn Sufi al-Himyari narrated to me, from Abdallah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Heedlessness is in three things: heedlessness of the remembrance of Allah, mighty and majestic is He; heedlessness from the time one prays the dawn prayer until the sun rises; and that a man be heedless of himself regarding debt until it mounts upon him."
"352","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Ma'ruf ibn Suwayd al-Judhami narrated to me, from Abu Ushshanah al-Ma'afiri, from Abdallah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Who is the first of the creation of Allah, mighty and majestic is He, to enter Paradise? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The first of the creation of Allah, mighty and majestic is He, to enter Paradise are the poor Emigrants, through whom the frontiers are guarded and through whom hardships are warded off; one of them dies with his need in his breast, unable to fulfill it. So Allah, mighty and majestic is He, says to whomever of His angels He wills: Go to them and greet them. The angels say: Our Lord, we are the dwellers of Your heaven and the best of Your creation, yet You command us to go to these and greet them with peace? He says: They were servants of Mine who worshipped Me and associated nothing with Me; through them the frontiers were guarded and through them hardships were warded off; one of them dies with his need in his breast, unable to fulfill it. So the angels come to them then, entering upon them from every gate: Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured; excellent is the final home."
"353","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Ka'b ibn Alqamah narrated to me, from Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi, from Abdallah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he mentioned the prayer one day and said: Whoever guards it, it will be a light, a proof, and a deliverance from the Fire for him on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever does not guard it, it will be neither a light, nor a proof, nor a deliverance for him, and on the Day of Resurrection he will be with Qarun, Pharaoh, Haman, and Ubayy ibn Khalaf."
"354","Abdallah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Ka'b ibn Alqamah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Abdallah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear the caller to prayer, say as he says, and send blessings upon me, for there is no one who sends blessings upon me but that Allah sends blessings upon him tenfold for it. And ask Allah for al-Wasilah for me, for al-Wasilah is a station in Paradise befitting none but a servant among the servants of Allah, mighty and majestic is He; I hope that I am he. Whoever asks it for me, my intercession becomes due for him."
"355","Husayn al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abdallah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Worship the Most Merciful, feed food, and spread peace; you will enter Paradise."
"356","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from Abdallah ibn Amr, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There are two traits which whoever guards will enter Paradise: whoever glorifies Allah ten times, magnifies Allah ten times, and praises Allah ten times at the end of every prayer, that is one hundred and fifty on the tongue and one thousand five hundred in the balance. He said: Which of you commits more than one thousand five hundred evil deeds in his day and night? He said: And I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counting them with his fingers. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how is it that we do not keep count of them? He said: Satan comes to one of you at the end of his prayer and reminds him of his needs, saying to him: Remember the need of such-and-such, until he leaves without having remembered; and he comes to him at his sleep and puts him to sleep without his having remembered."
"357","Ja'far ibn Awn informed us, Ayman ibn Nabil informed us, from Qudamah ibn Abdallah al-Amiri, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoning the pillar on the Day of Sacrifice, riding a tawny she-camel, with no beating, no driving away, and no cries of move away, move away."
"358","Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Alqamah ibn Waqqas, from Bilal ibn al-Harith: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may utter a word of the wrath of Allah, not realizing how far it reaches, and Allah, mighty and majestic is He, records His wrath against him for it until the day he meets Him; and a man may utter a word of the pleasure of Allah, not realizing how far it reaches, and Allah, mighty and majestic is He, records His pleasure for him for it until the day he meets Him."
"359","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would supplicate: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion."
"360","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah, and Bilal entered with him. I said to Bilal: Where did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: In the front of the House, with three cubits between him and the wall."
"361","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from a shaykh called al-Hafs, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: Bilal called the prayer during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he called it for Abu Bakr during his lifetime, but he did not call it in the time of Umar. Umar said to him: What keeps you from calling the prayer? He said: I called the prayer for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he passed away, and I called it for Abu Bakr until he passed away, for he was my benefactor; and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Bilal, there is no deed better than this deed of yours except striving in the path of Allah, mighty and majestic is He. So he went out to Syria and strove there."
"362","Yazid ibn Harun and Hibban ibn Hilal informed us, Amir ibn Salih narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No father has bestowed upon his child anything better than good manners."
"363","Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Burdah, from al-Agharr, who said: He said, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Turn to your Lord in repentance, for by Allah, I turn to my Lord, mighty and majestic is He, one hundred times a day."
"364","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Burdah, from al-Agharr, al-Agharr of Muzaynah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My heart is overcast every day, so that I seek the forgiveness of Allah one hundred times."
"365","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to me, Abdallah ibn Dawud narrated to us, saying: Salamah ibn Nubayt mentioned, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, from Nubayt ibn Sharit, from Salim ibn Ubayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill and lost consciousness, then recovered and said: Has the time of prayer come? We said: Yes. He said: Command Bilal to call the prayer and command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Then he lost consciousness and recovered and said: Has the time of prayer come? We said: Yes. He said: Command Bilal to call the prayer and command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Then he lost consciousness, and A'ishah said: My father is a tender-hearted man, so let him command another. Then he recovered and said: Has the prayer been established? They said: No. He said: Command Bilal to give the call to commence and command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. A'ishah said: My father is a tender-hearted man; if only you would command another. He said: You are like the companions of Joseph; command Bilal to call the prayer and command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. So Bilal gave the call and Abu Bakr stepped forward. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recovered and said: Find me someone to lean upon. So he came out leaning upon Barirah and another man until he sat beside Abu Bakr; Abu Bakr wanted to step back, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held him back, and Abu Bakr led the people in prayer. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, Umar said: I will not hear anyone say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has died but I will strike him with my sword. Salim ibn Ubayd said: Then they sent me, saying: Go to the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and call him. So I came to Abu Bakr while he was in the mosque, in a state of shock, and Abu Bakr said to me: Perhaps the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has died? I said: Umar says: I will not hear anyone say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has died but I will strike him with my sword. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up, took my arm, and I came with him. He said: Make room for me. So they made room for him. He bent over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), touched him, placed his hands, or his hand, and said: You are dead and they are dead. He said: O companion of the Messenger of Allah, has the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died? He said: Yes. So they knew it was as he said; they were an unlettered people among whom there had been no prophet before him. They said: O companion of the Messenger of Allah, shall we pray over him? He said: Yes. They said: How shall we pray over him? He said: A group will enter, magnify Allah, pray, and supplicate, then leave; then others will enter, until they finish. They said: O companion of the Messenger of Allah, shall he be buried? He said: Yes. They said: Where shall he be buried? He said: In the place where his soul was taken, for his soul was taken only in a goodly place. So they knew it was as he said. Then he went out and commanded them that his father's sons wash him. Then he went out and the Emigrants gathered to consult. They said: The Helpers have a share in this matter. So they went to them, and one of them said: From us an amir and from you an amir, for the Emigrants. Umar stood and said to them: Who has three things like what Abu Bakr has? The second of two when they were in the cave, who are they when he says to his companion: Do not grieve, Allah is with us? Who are they, with whom Allah, mighty and majestic is He, was? Then he took the hand of Abu Bakr and pledged allegiance to him, and the people pledged allegiance; it was a good and fine pledge."
"366","Abdallah ibn Yazid informed us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Bukayr ibn Abdallah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall strike more than ten lashes except in a prescribed punishment of Allah, mighty and majestic is He."
"367","Zakariyya ibn Adi informed me, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from one who informed him, from Abu Kathir, the freedman of Muhammad ibn Jahsh, from Muhammad ibn Jahsh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was walking in Madinah when he passed a man of Banu Adi called Ma'mar and said to him: Cover your thighs, for they are part of what must be covered. Then he sat and we sat. He raised his head to the sky, then placed his hand on his forehead and said: Glory be to Allah, what severity has been sent down! We were in awe of asking him. The next day we said: O Messenger of Allah, yesterday you said: What severity has been sent down, and we were in awe of asking you; what is it? He said: If a man were killed in the path of Allah, then brought to life, then killed, then brought to life, then killed, then brought to life, while a debt is upon him, he would not enter Paradise until his debt is repaid."
"368","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Ajlah narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, who said: When there was revealed: Allah and His angels send blessings upon the Prophet; O you who believe, send blessings upon him and greet him with peace, I stood up to him and said: Greeting we know, but how do we send blessings upon you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and upon the family of Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim; You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"369","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr al-Aqadi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq, from Abu Thumamah al-Hannat: that Ka'b ibn Ujrah met him while he was heading to the mosque, one of them meeting the other; he found me interlacing the fingers of one hand with the other, so he pulled my hands apart and forbade me that, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you performs ablution and performs it well, then goes out heading to the mosque, let him not interlace his fingers, for he is in prayer."
"370","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Asim al-Aqadi, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were sitting on a cushion of leather and said: After me there will be rulers; whoever enters upon them, believes their lies, and aids them in their wrongdoing is not of me and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Pond; and whoever does not believe their lies nor aid them in their wrongdoing is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Pond."
"371","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sa'd ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah narrated to me, from his father, from Ka'b, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were in the mosque, seven of us, three of us Arabs and four of our freedmen, or four of us Arabs and three of our freedmen. He came out to us from one of his rooms until he sat with us and said: What has seated you here? We said: Waiting for the prayer. He tapped the ground with his finger, then lowered his head for a while, then raised his head to us and said: Do you know what your Lord, mighty and majestic is He, has said? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: He says: Whoever prays the prayer at its time and observes its limits has a covenant from Me by which I shall admit him to Paradise; and whoever does not pray the prayer at its time nor observe its limits has no covenant with Me: if I will, I shall admit him to the Fire, and if I will, I shall admit him to Paradise."
"372","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Shu'bah narrated to us, Amr ibn Murrah informed me, saying: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrating from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, who said: Murrah ibn Ka'b, or Ka'b ibn Murrah, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against Mudar, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has given you and answered you, yet your people have perished; supplicate to Allah for them. He turned away from me, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has given you and answered you, yet your people have perished; supplicate to Allah for them to give them rain. He said: O Allah, give us a rescuing rain, wholesome, fruitful, abundant, encompassing, swift, not delaying, beneficial, not harmful. It was only a Friday or thereabouts before we were rained upon. He said: And he said to Murrah ibn Ka'b, or Ka'b: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may your father be for Allah, and beware. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire, a bone of his bones for every bone of his; and any Muslim man who frees two Muslim women, they will be his ransom from the Fire, a bone of his bones for every bone of both of them; and any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, she will be her ransom from the Fire, a bone of her bones for every bone of hers."
"373","Ja'far ibn Awn informed us, al-Mas'udi informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is like the tender stalk of a crop: the wind bends it, laying it down at times and straightening it at times, until his term comes to him; and the likeness of the disbeliever is like the firm cedar upon its root, which nothing uproots until its felling comes all at once."
"374","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr informed us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and Aws ibn Hadathan to announce during the days of Tashriq that none but the believer will enter Paradise, and that these are days of eating and drinking."
"375","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, that Ka'b said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seldom went out on a journey except on Thursday."
"376","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, who said: Umm Mubashshir said to Ka'b ibn Malik, while she was ill: Convey greetings to my son, meaning Mubashshir. He said: May Allah forgive you, O Umm Mubashshir, have you not heard what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The soul of the believer is a bird that feeds in the trees of Paradise until Allah returns it to his body on the Day of Resurrection? She said: I was mistaken, so I seek the forgiveness of Allah."
"377","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abdallah ibn Ka'b, from his father: that he demanded repayment of a debt owed to him by Ibn Abi Hadrad in the mosque, and their voices rose until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard them and came out to them. He said: O Ka'b, reduce this of your debt, gesturing to him by half. He said: I have done so. He said: Arise and pay him."
"378","Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muharibi narrated to me, Za'idah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Abu al-Yasar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or remits for him, Allah, mighty and majestic is He, will shade him in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His shade."
"379","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Ja'far, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah, from Uthman ibn Hunayf: that a blind man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Supplicate to Allah to cure me. He said: If you wish, I shall delay that, and it will be greater for your reward; and if you wish, I shall supplicate to Allah. He said: Supplicate to Him. So he commanded him to perform ablution, pray two cycles, and supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, I ask You and turn to You through Your Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Prophet of mercy; O Muhammad, I have turned through you to my Lord in this need of mine, that it be fulfilled; O Allah, grant him intercession for me."
"380","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Sufyan, from al-Jurayri, from Yazid ibn Abdallah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Satan has come between me and my prayer and my recitation. He said: That is a devil called Khanzab; when you sense him, seek refuge from him and spit to your left three times."
"381","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As: that he complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of whisperings in prayer. He said: That is a devil called Khanzab; when you sense anything of him, spit to your left three times and seek refuge in Allah from him."
"382","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to me, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Umar ibn Abdallah ibn Ka'b, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As al-Thaqafi: that he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a pain that had nearly disabled me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Place your right hand upon it, then say: In the name of Allah; I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of what I feel, seven times. I did that, and Allah, mighty and majestic is He, cured me."
"383","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Abdallah ibn Idris narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ja'dah ibn Hubayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them; then the last are the worst."
"384","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Layth, from Talhah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution: he placed his hand upon his head, then drew it back over his nape, then brought it out from beneath the chin."
"385","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Jamil, from Nafi' ibn Abd al-Harith, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the happiness of a man is a spacious dwelling, a righteous neighbor, and a comfortable mount."
"386","Safwan ibn Isa informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa': that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray the sunset prayer at the hour the sun set, when its upper edge had disappeared."
"387","Uthman ibn Umar informed us, Umar ibn Rashid informed us, from Iyas ibn Salamah, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would begin his supplication with: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, the Bestower."
"388","Hashim ibn al-Qasim informed us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, Iyas ibn Salamah informed us, from his father: that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to a man called Busr ibn Ra'i al-Ir of Ashja', while he was eating with his left hand: Eat with your right. He said: I cannot. He said: May you never be able. He said: It never reached his mouth afterwards."
"389","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Salamah ibn Nu'aym, who was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets Allah, exalted is He, associating nothing with Him will enter Paradise, even if he commits adultery and even if he steals."
"390","Husayn al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Mansur, from al-Musayyab, from Warrad, who said: al-Mughirah wrote to Mu'awiyah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say when he finished the prayer: There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what You give, none gives what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You."
"391","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, Warrad, the scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, narrated to me, saying: Mu'awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah: Write to me something of the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he wrote to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seek refuge from three: disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding and demanding; and I heard him forbid three: gossip, wasting wealth, and excessive asking. He said: And I heard him say: O Allah, none withholds what You give, none repels what You decree, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You."
"392","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Warrad, the scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, who said: Sa'd ibn Ubadah said: If I saw a man with my wife, I would strike him with the sword without sparing. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do you marvel at the jealousy of Sa'd? By Allah, I am more jealous than he, and Allah, mighty and majestic is He, is more jealous than I; and because of the jealousy of Allah He forbade shameful deeds, what is apparent of them and what is hidden. No person loves excuse more than Allah, mighty and majestic is He; for that reason He sent messengers as bearers of glad tidings and warners. And no person loves His praise more than Allah, mighty and majestic is He; for that reason Allah promised Paradise."
"393","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Aqqar ibn al-Mughirah, that is Ibn Shu'bah, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is cauterized or seeks an incantation has disowned reliance."
"394","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Nu'man ibn Sa'd, from al-Mughirah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The slogan of the Muslims on the Bridge on the Day of Resurrection is: My Lord, grant safety; my Lord, grant safety."
"395","Abu Nu'aym informed us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin, Amr ibn Wahb al-Thaqafi narrated to me, from al-Mughirah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieved himself, he went far away."
"396","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman and Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wa'il, from al-Mughirah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the rubbish heap of so-and-so's tribe, parted his legs, and urinated standing."
"397","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar and Ibn Jurayj informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Ziyad, from Urwah ibn al-Mughirah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; when he was on part of the road, he withdrew and I withdrew with him carrying the water vessel. He relieved himself, then came to me and I poured water over his hands, at the time of the dawn prayer. When he washed his face and wanted to wash his forearms, the sleeves of his cloak were too tight, and upon him was a Syrian cloak, so he brought his hands out from beneath the cloak and washed his forearms, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. He said: Then we reached the people, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf had already led them in one cycle. I went to inform him, but he said: Leave him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one cycle with him, then left; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed one cycle, and the people were startled by that. He said: You did right, or he said: You did well, commending them for praying the prayer at its time."
"398","al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad informed us, from Sufyan, from Abu Qays, from al-Hudhayl ibn Shurahbil, from al-Mughirah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over his socks and his sandals."
"399","Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinate while standing, then I poured water for him, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"400","Umar ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Salil, from Mujibah al-Bahili, from his uncle, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Do you recognize me? I am the one who came to you the year before. He mentioned his fine physique and said: I have not broken fast by day since you, except by night. He said: And who commanded you to torment yourself? Fast the month of patience and one day of the month. He said: I am stronger than that. He said: Fast the month of patience and two days of the month. He said: I am stronger than that. He said: Fast the month of patience and three days of the month. He said: I am stronger than that. He said: Fast the sacred months and break fast."
"401","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad entered upon Ma'qil ibn Yasar to visit him while ill, and we were with him, Ibn Ziyad being the governor, and he questioned him. Ma'qil said: By Allah, I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); by Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any man whom Allah puts in charge of subjects and who dies on the day he dies while deceiving his subjects, Allah will forbid him Paradise. He said: Why did you not narrate this to me before today? He said: Had I not seen my condition, I would not have narrated it to you."
"402","Rawh ibn Ubadah and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Worship in times of turmoil is like emigration to me."
"403","Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Iyad, who said: I heard Ma'qil say: There was a dispute between two of his neighbors over a boundary, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath by which he severs the property of his brother will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"404","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Habib ibn Abi Jubayrah, from Ya'la ibn al-Sayyabah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave whose occupant was being punished and said: The occupant of this grave is being punished for no great matter. Then he called for a palm stalk, placed it upon his grave, and said: Perhaps it will lighten for him so long as it remains moist."
"405","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abdallah ibn Hafs, from Ya'la ibn Murrah al-Thaqafi, who said: Three things I saw of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): While we were traveling with him, we passed a camel used for drawing water. When the camel saw him, it grumbled and lowered its load. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped by it and said: Where is the owner of this camel? He came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sell it to me. He said: Rather I shall give it to you. He said: Rather sell it to me. He said: Rather I shall give it to you, though it belongs to a household that has no livelihood but it. He said: Since you have mentioned this of its condition, it has complained of much work and little fodder, so treat it well. Then we traveled and alighted at a stopping place, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept. A tree came, splitting the earth until it covered him, then returned to its place. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke, I told him, and he said: It is a tree that asked its Lord's permission to greet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and He permitted it. Then we traveled and passed a watering place, and a woman came to him with a son of hers afflicted with madness. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him by the nose and said: Come out, for I am Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then we traveled, and when we returned from our journey we passed that watering place, and the woman came to him with a slaughter camel and milk. He commanded her to take back the slaughter camel and commanded his Companions, who drank the milk. He asked her about the boy, and she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, we have seen no trouble from him since you."
"406","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Abu Ya'fur, from Ayman, who said: I heard Ya'la al-Thaqafi say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever takes land without its right will be charged with carrying its soil to the gathering place."
"407","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from al-Rabi' ibn Abdallah, from Ayman ibn Nabil, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any man who wrongfully takes a handspan of land, Allah will charge him with digging it until he reaches the bottom of the seven earths, then it will be hung upon his neck until the Day of Resurrection, until judgment is passed among the people."
"408","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Hariz ibn Uthman informed us, Abu al-Hasan al-Hawzani, Nimran ibn Mikhmar al-Rahabi, narrated to us, from Shurahbil ibn Aws al-Kindi, who was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he drinks it again, flog him; if he drinks it again, flog him; if he drinks it a fourth time, kill him."
"409","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Bahz ibn Hakim informed us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You complete seventy nations; you are the last of them and the noblest of them to Allah, mighty and majestic is He."
"410","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Hakim ibn Mu'awiyah al-Qushayri, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In Paradise there is a sea of water, a sea of milk, a sea of honey, and a sea of wine; then the rivers split off from them afterwards."
"411","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to me, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Jurayri narrating from Hakim ibn Mu'awiyah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You complete seventy nations; you are the best of them and the noblest of them to Allah, mighty and majestic is He. Between the two leaves of a gate of Paradise is a journey of forty years, and there will come a day upon it when it is crowded."
"412","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Shu'bah, saying: Jarad informed me, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Mu'awiyah: that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: For whomever Allah wills good, He gives him understanding of the religion."
"413","Abu Usamah informed us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Abu Mijlaz, Lahiq ibn Humayd, who said: Mu'awiyah entered a house in which were Abdallah ibn Amir and Abdallah ibn al-Zubayr. Abdallah ibn Amir stood, but Abdallah ibn al-Zubayr did not stand. Mu'awiyah said to Abdallah ibn Amir: Sit, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever loves that men stand for him, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"414","Yahya ibn Bishr narrated to me, al-Hakam ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, Ibn Jabir informed us, Abu Abd Rabbihi narrated to me, saying: I heard Mu'awiyah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Deeds are like a vessel: when its top is good, its bottom is good, and when its top is corrupt, its bottom is corrupt."
"415","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Mu'awiyah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Nothing befalls the believer in his body that hurts him but that some of his evil deeds are expiated by it."
"416","Ya'la narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, who said: I heard Mu'awiyah preaching, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon these pieces of wood: O Allah, none withholds what You give, none gives what You withhold; for whomever Allah wills good, He gives him understanding of the religion."
"417","Uthman said: And Ziyad, the freedman of al-Harith, narrated to me the like of this hadith, adding therein: And the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You."
"418","Ya'la narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Isa ibn Talhah, who said: I heard Mu'awiyah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The callers to prayer will be the longest-necked of people on the Day of Resurrection."
"419","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, that Abu Shaykh al-Huna'i said: I was among a company of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with Mu'awiyah, and Mu'awiyah said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing silk? They said: O Allah, yes, and I bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from silver vessels? They said: O Allah, yes, and I bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade riding upon the spotted skins of leopards? They said: O Allah, yes, and I bear witness. He said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade combining Hajj and Umrah? They said: As for this, no. He said: Yet it is among them."
"420","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, saying: Ibn Munabbih narrated to me, from his brother, that he heard Mu'awiyah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not press me insistently in asking. By Allah, no one presses me insistently and I give him but that what I gave him is blessed for him."
"421","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Amir al-Bajali narrating from Jarir ibn Abdallah, who said: I heard Mu'awiyah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died at sixty-three years of age; Abu Bakr died at sixty-three years of age; Umar died at sixty-three years of age; and I am sixty-three years of age."
"422","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Pray the dawn prayer at daybreak, for it is greater in reward."
"423","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Asim ibn Umar, from Rafi', who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The worker in charity, for the sake of Allah, in truth, is like the warrior in the path of Allah until he returns to his family."
"424","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Masruq narrated to us, from Abayah ibn Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' ibn Khadij, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Fever is a blast from the Fire, so cool it with water."
"425","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abayah ibn Rifa'ah, from his grandfather Rafi' ibn Khadij, who said: Gabriel, or an angel, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: How do you count those of you who witnessed Badr? They said: The best of us. He said: Likewise they are with us, the best of the angels."
"426","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Abu al-Najashi, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, who said: We would pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then a slaughter camel would be sacrificed, divided into ten portions, then cooked, then we would eat well-cooked meat before praying the sunset prayer."
"427","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, al-Awza'i informed us, Abu al-Najashi informed us, Rafi' ibn Khadij narrated to me, who said: We would pray the sunset prayer in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of us would leave and could still see the places where his arrows landed."
"428","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Iyad narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating to us, saying: I heard Layla, the wife of Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyyah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Bashir, whereas his name before that was Zahm, say: Bashir informed me that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, shall I fast on Friday and speak to no one that day? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast on Friday except among days of which it is one, or a month; as for not speaking, by my life, that you speak, enjoining right and forbidding wrong, is better than that you remain silent."
"429","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Iyad narrated to us, saying: Iyad narrated to me, from Layla, the wife of Bashir, who said: I wanted to fast two days continuously, but Bashir prevented me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it. He said: The Christians do that; rather fast as Allah commanded you, and complete the fast until night, and when night comes, break fast."
"430","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abdallah ibn al-Ayzar informed us, from a man of the people of Syria: that Umar wanted to appoint Bishr ibn Asim, who said: I shall not work for you. He said: Why? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The ruler will be brought and made to stand upon the Bridge; it will shake with him until every limb of his moves from its place. If he was just, he will pass; if he was unjust, he will plunge into the Fire for seventy autumns. So Umar entered the mosque with a changed color, and Abu Dharr said to him: What is the matter with you, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: A hadith narrated to me by Bishr ibn Asim. He said: And what is it? So he narrated it to him, and Abu Dharr said: Yes, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say it. Umar said: And who would desire office after this? Abu Dharr said: One whose nose Allah has rubbed in the dust and whose cheek He has humbled."
"431","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Sawadah, from Anas ibn Malik, a man of Banu Abdallah ibn Ka'b, who said: The cavalry of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided us and took the camels of a neighbor of ours. I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found him eating. He said: Come and eat. I said: I am fasting. He said: Come, I shall tell you about that: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, has lifted half the prayer and fasting from the traveler, and from the pregnant and nursing woman. Then he said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said them both, or one of them. He would say: How I wish I had eaten of the food of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"432","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, from Umarah ibn Hadid al-Bajali, narrating from Sakhr al-Ghamidi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my nation in their early mornings. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent out a detachment, he sent them at the beginning of the day. Sakhr was a merchant, and when he sent out his lads, he sent them at the beginning of the day. His wealth grew until he did not know where to put it."
"433","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Dirghamah ibn Ulaybah ibn Harmalah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prayed the dawn prayer with him. When he finished the prayer, I looked at the faces of the people; their faces were scarcely discernible after I had finished the prayer. When I was about to depart, I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Upon you is fear of Allah, mighty and majestic is He; when you rise from among people and hear them say to you what pleases you, do it, and what you hear them say to you of what you dislike, leave it. He said: My father Ulaybah was dutiful to his father Harmalah. I said: And what was his dutifulness to him? He said: When food was brought near, he would look for the fullest, tastiest bone and give it to him; and when traveling, he would look for the smoothest, finest camel and mount him upon it. That was his dutifulness to him."
"434","Amr ibn Awn narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Khalid ibn Abdallah al-Qasri, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Yazid ibn Asad, love for people what you love for yourself."
"435","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Imran al-Qasir, who said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman informed me, from Yazid ibn Na'amah al-Dabbi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man befriends a man, let him ask him his name, his father's name, and from whom he is, for it is a stronger bond of affection."
"436","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Sa'id ibn Ashwa', from Yazid ibn Salamah: that he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have heard much hadith from you, and I fear the first of it will make me forget the last of it; narrate to me a word that will be comprehensive. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear Allah in what you know."
"437","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Abdallah ibn al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall take the property of his companion, seriously or in jest; and when one of you finds his companion's stick, let him return it to him."
"438","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Hakim ibn Abi Yazid, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave people, that some of them may benefit from others; when a man seeks counsel from a man, let him advise him sincerely."
"439","Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to me, Sa'id ibn al-Sa'ib al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, my father al-Sa'ib ibn Yasar narrated to me, saying: I heard Yazid ibn Amir al-Suwa'i, who had witnessed Hunayn with the polytheists then embraced Islam; we would ask him about the terror Allah, mighty and majestic is He, cast into the hearts of the polytheists on the day of Hunayn, how it was. He said: He would take a pebble for us and throw it at a basin, and it would ring. We would find in our bellies something like that."
"440","Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, Sa'id ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yasar, from Yazid ibn Amir, who said: At a rout in which the Muslims were routed on the day of Hunayn, the disbelievers pursued them. The Messenger of Allah took a handful of earth, then turned with it upon the polytheists and threw it in their faces, saying: Return; may the faces be disfigured. There was none who met his brother but that he complained of grit or wiped his eyes."
"441","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, who said: Yazid ibn Shajarah stood among his companions and said: Morning and evening have come upon you, between green, red, and yellow, and in the houses is what there is; when you meet the enemy tomorrow, then forward, forward. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No man steps forward a step but that the wide-eyed maidens advance toward him; if they hold back from him, and if he is martyred, his first spurt of blood is expiation for his sins; two of the wide-eyed maidens descend to him, shake the dust from him, and say: Welcome, your time has come; and he says: Welcome, your time has come."
"442","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Nafi' ibn Umar al-Jumahi informed us, from Umayyah ibn Safwan, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Thaqafi, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at al-Banah, or al-Banawah, and al-Banawah is of Ta'if, saying: You are about to know the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire, or he said: Your best from your worst. I know only that he said: The people of Paradise from the Fire. They said: O Messenger of Allah, by what? He said: By good praise and evil praise; you are witnesses, some of you over others."
"443","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abdallah ibn Qays, from al-Harith ibn Waqsh, or Wuqaysh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two Muslims lose four of their children but that Allah admits them to Paradise by His mercy. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and three? He said: And three. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and two? He said: And two. He said: Among my nation is one who will be immense for the Fire, so as to be one of its corners; and among my nation is one through whose intercession more than Mudar will enter Paradise."
"444","Al-Hasan ibn Musa informed us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Habib ibn Abi Subay'ah al-Duba'i, from al-Harith: that a man was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man passed by. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I love him for Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you informed him of that? He said: No. He said: Go and inform him. So he went and said: I love you for Allah. He said: May He whom you love me for love you."
"445","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Saksaki narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal al-Madani, from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Jahm, from al-Harith ibn Malik al-Ansari: that he passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said to him: O Harith, how have you woken? He said: I have woken a true believer. He said: Consider what you say, for every truth has a reality. He said: Have I not turned the world away from myself, made my day thirsty, kept my night awake, and it is as though I look upon the Throne of my Lord manifest, as though I look upon the people of Paradise visiting one another therein, and as though I look upon the people of the Fire wailing therein, meaning crying out? He said: O Harith, you have known, so hold fast, three times."
"446","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Abdallah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah informed me, from Harithah ibn al-Nu'man, who said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Gabriel was sitting with him in the seating places. I greeted him, then passed on. When I returned and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left, he said: Did you see the one who was with me? I said: Yes. He said: He was Gabriel, upon him be peace, and he returned your greeting."
"447","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Waqid ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd, that he heard Safwan narrating from Muhammad ibn Sahl, from his father, or from Muhammad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you prays toward something, let him draw near to it, lest Satan cut off his prayer."
"448","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi: that a man looked through a hole in the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was scratching his head with a comb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I known you were looking at me, I would have thrust it into your eye. Seeking permission was made only because of seeing."
"449","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd: that Uhud shook while upon it were the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be firm, Uhud; upon you are none but a prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs."
"450","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Abu Hazim, who said: I was with Sahl ibn Sa'd when it was said to him: There was something between Banu Amr ibn Awf and the people of Quba. He said: That was long ago. We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when word came to him that there had been something among the people of Quba, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to make peace between them, and was delayed from the people. Bilal said to Abu Bakr: Shall I establish the prayer? He said: As you wish. Bilal established it, and the people put Abu Bakr forward. While he was praying, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, making his way through the rows until he stood behind Abu Bakr. They began to clap, but Abu Bakr would not turn in prayer. When they increased, he turned, and there was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing behind him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to pray as he was, but Abu Bakr stepped back and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and prayed. When he finished, he said to Abu Bakr: What kept you, when I commanded you, from continuing to pray? He said: It does not befit the son of Abu Quhafah to lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this clapping in prayer? Clapping is for women, and glorifying Allah is for men."
"451","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while some of his Companions were with him. She moved among them but found no place, so a man made room for her; he stood and she sat and relieved her need, then stood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know her? He said: No. He said: Did you show her mercy, may Allah have mercy upon you, three times."
"452","Yazid ibn Abi Hakim informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam al-Madani narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In this nation there will be swallowing by the earth, transformation, and pelting. It was said: And when is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When singing girls and musical instruments appear and wines are deemed lawful."
"453","Abdallah ibn Maslamah narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl ibn Sa'd: that he was asked about the wound of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud. He said: The face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wounded, his front tooth broken, and the helmet crushed upon his head. Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would wash the blood, and Ali would pour water over her upon the shield. When Fatimah saw that the water only increased the blood, she took a piece of mat, burned it until it became ash, and pressed it to the wound, and the blood was staunched."
"454","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, saying: Abu Hazim ibn Dinar narrated to me, saying: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: We would take neither lunch nor midday rest on Friday except after Friday prayer."
"455","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, saying: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, saying: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a gate called al-Rayyan, through which the fasting will enter on the Day of Resurrection; none but they will enter through it. It will be said: Where are the fasting? They will stand and enter through it; when the last of them has entered, it will be closed, and none will enter through it."
"456","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, saying: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, Abu Hazim narrated to me, saying: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning outing one of you makes in the path of Allah, or an evening outing, is better than the world and what is in it; and the space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"457","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, saying: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, saying: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise as it appears to people while he is among the people of Hell, and another may do the deeds of the people of Hell as it appears to people while he is among the people of Paradise."
"458","Amr ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Ummah will remain upon good as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast."
"459","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to me, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl ibn Sa'd: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met the polytheists in one of his campaigns and they fought, and each people withdrew to their camp, and among the Muslims was a man who left no isolated or scattered group of the polytheists except that he pursued it and struck it with his sword. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, today no one has sufficed as so-and-so has sufficed. He said: Yet he is among the people of Hell. The people deemed that grave and said: Which of us is among the people of Paradise if so-and-so is among the people of Hell? A man from the people said: By Allah, he will never die upon this state. He followed him; whenever he hastened he hastened with him, and when he slowed he slowed with him, until the man was wounded and his wounds became severe, so he hastened death: he placed the hilt of his sword on the ground and its tip between his breasts, then threw himself upon it and killed himself. The man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: And what is that? He informed him of what had happened. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise as it appears to people while he is among the people of Hell, and he may do the deeds of the people of Hell as it appears to people while he is among the people of Paradise."
"460","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to me, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand - or seven hundred thousand, Abu Hazim said: I do not know which of the two - of my Ummah will enter Paradise, holding onto one another, each grasping the hand of the other; the first of them will not enter until the last of them enters, their faces like the moon on the night of fullness."
"461","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to me, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, that he heard Sahl ibn Sa'd being asked: Did you see fine white flour in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I never saw fine flour until Allah took His Messenger. I said: Did you have sieves in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I never saw a sieve until Allah took His Messenger. I said: Did you eat barley unsifted? He said: Yes; we would blow on it and what flew away flew, and what remained we moistened and ate."
"462","Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to me, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl ibn Sa'd: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a woven cloak that had its border in it. Then Sahl said: Do you know what a burdah is? They said: Yes, a shamlah (a woolen wrap). He said: Yes, it is the shamlah. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I wove this with my hand and have come to clothe you with it. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it as he was in need of it, and he came out to us wearing it as his waist-wrap. He said: So-and-so, son of so-and-so - touching it - naming a man, said: O Messenger of Allah, how fine this cloak is; clothe me with it. He said: Yes. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, he folded it and sent it to him. The people said to him: By Allah, you did not do well; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was clothed with it as he was in need of it, then you asked him for it although you knew he does not turn away any asker. He said: By Allah, I did not ask him for it to wear it; I asked him for it only so that it may be my shroud on the day I die. Sahl said: And it was his shroud on the day he died."
"463","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Hazim say: I heard Sahl ibn Sa'd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Paradise and said: In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and what has never occurred to the heart of a human."
"464","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Abu Hafs al-Ta'ifi, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts the Day of Arafah is forgiven for two consecutive years."
"465","Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, saying: Ayyash ibn Uqbah narrated to us, saying: I heard Yahya ibn Maymun al-Hadrami say: Sahl ibn Sa'd stopped by us while we were in the mosque, and Sahl said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever sits in the mosque awaiting the prayer is engaged in prayer."
"466","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from his brother, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were reciting the Qur'an to one another, and he said: Praise be to Allah; the Book of Allah is one, and among you are the virtuous, and among you are the red and the black. Then he said: Recite, recite, recite, before there come peoples who will set up its letters as the arrow is set up, not passing beyond their collarbones; they will hasten its reward and will not await it."
"467","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Waki' narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Uthman, saying: Imran ibn Abi Anas narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: Two men differed in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the mosque founded upon piety: one of them said it is the mosque of Medina, and the other said it is the mosque of Quba. They came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It is this mosque of mine."
"468","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from his father, from Sahl ibn Hunayf: He asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhi (pre-seminal fluid), and he said: Ablution suffices you for it. He said: And what do I do about what has touched my garment? He said: Take a handful of water and sprinkle your garment where you think it touched."
"469","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, saying: Yusuf ibn Tahman informed me, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution well, then comes to the mosque of Quba and prays four rak'ahs in it, that is equal to an Umrah."
"470","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Ya'qub ibn Zayd, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: Peace be upon you, ten good deeds are written for him; and whoever says: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, twenty good deeds are written for him; and whoever says: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, thirty good deeds are written for him."
"471","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abdullah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever helps a warrior in the path of Allah, or a debtor in his hardship, or a contractual slave regarding his manumission, Allah will shade him on a Day when there is no shade but His."
"472","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri narrated to me, from his father, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Suhayl ibn al-Bayda, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out one night while I was riding behind him, saying: O Suhayl ibn al-Bayda, raising his voice. I said: At your service, raising my voice with it until those behind us and before us heard it, and they gathered, knowing that he intended to say something. He said: Whoever says: There is no deity but Allah, Allah will thereby make Paradise obligatory for him and free him from the Fire."
"473","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, saying: Busr ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me, from Abu Idris, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', from Abu Marthad, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not sit upon graves, and do not pray facing them."
"474","Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ushara narrated to us, from his father, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is slaughter only from the labbah (the hollow of the throat) and the throat? He said: If you had stabbed her in the thigh it would have sufficed you."
"475","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to me, saying: Abu Dawud al-Subay'i narrated to me, saying: Abu al-Hamra narrated to me, saying: I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for nine months; whenever morning came he would come to the door of Ali and Fatimah, saying: May Allah have mercy on you: Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly."
"476","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, from Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Imran ibn Husayn, from his father, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, Abd al-Muttalib was better to his people than you; he fed them liver and hump while you slaughter them. He replied to him whatever Allah willed. When he intended to leave, he said: What shall I say? He said: Say: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul and decree for me the most rightly-guided of my affair. He left without having embraced Islam, then he embraced Islam and said: O Messenger of Allah, I had come to you and said: Teach me, and you said: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul and decree for me the most rightly-guided of my affair; so what shall I say now that I have embraced Islam? He said: Say: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul and decree for me the most rightly-guided of my affair; O Allah, forgive me what I concealed and what I announced, what I erred in and what I did deliberately, and what I did ignorantly."
"477","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Harithah ibn Wahb al-Khuza'i, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise: every weak one, deemed weak - if he were to swear by Allah, He would fulfill it. Shall I not inform you of the people of Hell: every harsh, arrogant one."
"478","Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Harithah ibn Wahb, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity, for there will come upon you a time when a man will give charity and find no one to accept it."
"479","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, saying: I heard Harithah ibn Wahb say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity; it is imminent that a man will go out with his charity and find no one to accept it."
"480","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Harithah ibn Wahb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The jawwaz (the coarse, miserly hoarder) will not enter Paradise, nor the ja'zari (the arrogant, bulky one). And the jawwaz is the harsh, coarse one."
"481","Zayd ibn Hubab al-Ukli narrated to us, saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr informed me, from his father, saying: I heard Amr ibn al-Hamiq say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends good for a servant, He sweetens him (asalahu). It was said: And what is His sweetening him? He said: He opens for him a righteous deed before his death until those around him are pleased with him."
"482","Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani informed us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi informed me, from Abu Shurayh al-Adawi of Khuza'ah, who was among the Companions, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days, and his prize (honored portion) is a day and a night; and it is not lawful for any of you to stay with his brother until he makes him sinful. He said: I said: And what makes him sinful? He said: He stays with him while he has nothing with which to honor him."
"483","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Rejoice, rejoice; do you not testify that there is no deity but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: Yes. He said: Then this Qur'an is a rope whose one end is in the Hand of Allah and whose other end is in your hands, so hold fast to it, for you will never go astray nor perish after it, ever."
"484","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Abu Aqil al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid and Atiyyah ibn Qays, from Atiyyah al-Sa'di, who was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The servant will not attain being among the God-fearing until he abandons what is harmless out of caution for what is harmful."
"485","Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam informed us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, from Urwah ibn Muhammad, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The giving upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"486","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Sufyan ibn al-Hakam - or al-Hakam ibn Sufyan: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he performed ablution and finished his ablution, would take a handful of water and sprinkle it beneath himself."
"487","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi, who said: I am the first who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid that a man urinate facing the qiblah. He said: So I went out to the people and informed them."
"488","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, saying: al-Ajlah narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to us: Do not benefit from the carcass by (using) hide or sinew."
"489","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, that a woman used to pick up reeds and filth from the mosque and then died; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by her grave and prayed over her."
"490","Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam informed us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abdullah ibn Adi ibn al-Hamra: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was sitting among people, a man came to him asking permission to confide with him about killing a man from the hypocrites. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke his words aloud and said: Does he not testify that there is no deity but Allah? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but he has no testimony. He said: Does he not testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but he has no testimony. He said: Does he not pray? He said: Yes, but he has no prayer. He said: Those are the ones I have been forbidden to kill."
"491","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri informed me, saying: My father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, saying: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Abdullah ibn Adi ibn al-Hamra informed him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was standing upon his mount at al-Hazwarah in Mecca, saying to Mecca: By Allah, you are the best of Allah's land and the most beloved of Allah's land to me; had I not been expelled from you I would not have left."
"492","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri narrated to me, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from his uncle, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud informed me that Shibl ibn Khulayd al-Muzani informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the slave-girl: If she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, flog her; then if she commits adultery, sell her even for a rope - and the rope (dafir) is a cord - on the third or the fourth time."
"493","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir, from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ansari, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Maghrib: By the fig and the olive."
"494","Ibn Abi Fudayk informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Barrad, from Mu'adh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb, from his father, who said: We went out on a rainy, intensely dark, severe night, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sought to pray for us. He said: I found him, and he said: Say. I said nothing. Then he said: Say. I said nothing. He said: Say. I said: O Messenger of Allah, and what shall I say? He said: Say: He is Allah, the One, and the two refuge-seeking chapters, when you enter evening and when you enter morning, three times; they will suffice you against everything."
"495","Husayn al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Razin, from Ibn Umm Maktum, who said: I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I am old, blind, far from home, and I have a guide who does not suit me; do you find any concession for me? He said: Do you hear the call? I said: Yes. He said: I find no concession for you."
"496","Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to me, from Awf, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abdullah ibn Salam, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, the people looked out for him; they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come. He said: So I went out among those who went out, and when I saw his face I knew it was not the face of a liar. The first thing I heard him say was: O people, spread peace, feed food, pray while people sleep, and enter Paradise in peace."
"497","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, who said: I came to Medina and sat with some elders in the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and an old man came leaning upon a staff of his. The people said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man from the people of Paradise, let him look at this one. He said: So he stood behind a pillar and prayed two rak'ahs. I went to him and said to him: Some people said such-and-such. He said: Paradise belongs to Allah, Mighty and Majestic; He admits into it whom He wills. I saw a dream in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I saw as though a man came to me and said to me: Go, so I went with him, and he took me along a great path. A road appeared to me on my left and I intended to take it, but he said: You are not among its people. Then a road appeared to me on my right and I took it until I reached a slippery mountain; he took my hand and pushed me up, and I was upon its peak, and I could neither settle nor hold firm. There was an iron pillar upon its peak with a ring of gold; he took my hand and pushed me up until I grasped the handhold. He said: Hold fast. I said: Yes. He struck the pillar with his foot while I held fast to the handhold. I related it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You have seen good: as for the great path, it is the gathering place; as for the road that appeared on your left, it is the road of the people of Hell and you are not among its people; as for the road that appeared on your right, it is the road of the people of Paradise; as for the slippery mountain, it is the station of the martyrs; and as for the handhold you grasped, it is the handhold of Islam, so hold fast to it until you die. So I hope to be among the people of Paradise - and he was Abdullah ibn Salam."
"498","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Yahya ibn Ya'la al-Taymi Abu al-Muhayyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from the nephew of Abdullah ibn Salam, from Abdullah ibn Salam, who said: My name in the pre-Islamic period was so-and-so, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Abdullah ibn Salam."
"499","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on Friday and said: It would be no burden upon any of you to buy two garments for his Friday apart from the garment of his work."
"500","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Abu Na'amah, that Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani heard his son saying: O Allah, I ask You for al-Firdaws, and I ask You, and I ask You. Abdullah said to him: Ask Allah for Paradise and seek refuge with Him from the Fire, for I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be among this Ummah a people who transgress in supplication and purification."
"501","Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you come upon the resting places of camels, do not pray in them; and when you come upon the resting places of sheep, pray in them if you wish."
"502","Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog that is not a hunting dog, nor a sheepdog, nor a farm dog, then a qirat is deducted from his reward every day."
"503","Sa'id ibn Amir and Hawdhah narrated to us, from Awf, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that dogs are a community among communities, I would have ordered that they be killed; so kill from them every jet-black one."
"504","Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yunus and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness, and gives upon it what He does not give upon harshness."
"505","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, saying: Ash'ath ibn Abdullah informed me, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you urinate in his bathing place and then perform ablution in it, for most whisperings (of Satan) come from it."
"506","Yazid ibn Harun informed me, saying: Hariz ibn Uthman al-Rahabi narrated to us, saying: I said to Abdullah ibn Busr: Was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) an old man? He said: On his chin were a few white hairs."
"507","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Abdullah ibn Busr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to my father and stayed with him; he brought him food, and haysah (a dish of dates, cheese and clarified butter), sawiq and dates. Then he brought him drink and he drank and passed to the one on his right. He said: And he would eat dates, placing the stones upon the back of his two fingers, the index and the middle, and throw them. Then he said: O Allah, bless them in what You have provided them, forgive them and have mercy on them."
"508","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Thawr, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abdullah ibn Busr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fast on Saturday except what has been obligated upon you; and if one of you finds nothing but a grape stalk or the bark of a tree, let him chew it."
"509","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih informed me, saying: Amr ibn Qays narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Busr al-Khuza'i, that a Bedouin said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which of the people is best? He said: The one whose life is long and whose deed is good."
"510","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Asim al-Ahwal informed us, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled, he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the hardship of travel, the gloom of return, decrease after increase, the supplication of the oppressed, and an evil sight concerning family and wealth. Yazid said: I heard it from Asim, and Shu'bah confirmed it to me."
"511","Sulayman ibn Harb and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed me, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he traveled, would say: O Allah, You are the Companion in travel and the Successor over family. O Allah, accompany us in our travel and succeed us over our family. O Allah, we seek refuge with You from the hardship of travel and the gloom of return; and I seek refuge with You from decrease after increase, the supplication of the oppressed, and an evil sight concerning family and wealth. Muhammad ibn al-Fadl added in his narration, saying: Asim was asked about decrease after increase; he said: They say: he declined after he had been upright."
"512","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Imran narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis al-Muzani, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deliberateness, moderation, and good composure are one part of twenty-four parts of prophethood."
"513","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, who said: I reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after there had been revealed upon him: Rivalry has distracted you, while he was reciting: Rivalry has distracted you, and saying: The son of Adam says: My wealth, my wealth; and have you of your wealth except what you gave in charity and sent forth, or ate and consumed, or wore and wore out?"
"514","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Mutarrif, from his father, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and his chest had a sound like the boiling of a cauldron."
"515","Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, saying: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, from Shaddad ibn Sa'id al-Rasibi Abu Talhah, saying: Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to me, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, sitting and standing, reciting: Rivalry has distracted you, until he completed it."
"516","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) go out seeking rain; he turned his back to the people, faced the qiblah, turned his cloak inside out, began supplicating, prayed two rak'ahs and recited aloud."
"517","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from his uncle, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reclining in the mosque, raising one leg over the other."
"518","Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Tamim al-Ansari, from Abdullah ibn Zayd, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Ibrahim declared Mecca sacred and supplicated for it; and I have declared Medina sacred as Ibrahim declared Mecca sacred, and I have supplicated for it regarding its mudd and sa' with the like of what Ibrahim supplicated for Mecca."
"519","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, saying: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, that Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him: A man from the Ansar disputed with al-Zubayr before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the streams of al-Harrah with which they watered the palms, and al-Zubayr refused him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water, O Zubayr, then send on to your neighbor. The Ansari became angry and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it because he is the son of your aunt?! The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed color, then he said: Water, O Zubayr, then hold back the water until it returns to the embankment. Al-Zubayr said: By Allah, I consider this verse was revealed concerning that: But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what has arisen between them - the verse."
"520","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling and two sucklings do not prohibit (marriage)."
"521","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Habib al-Mu'allim, from Ata, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the Sacred Mosque; and a prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a prayer in this mosque of mine by a hundred prayers."
"522","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, saying: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from bowing, he would say: Allah hears the one who praises Him; O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything thereafter."
"523","Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, saying: I said to Ibn Abi Awfa: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicate against the Confederates? He said: Yes. He said: O Allah, Sender of the Book, Swift in reckoning, Defeater of the Confederates; O Allah, defeat the Confederates and shake them."
"524","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Wasiti, from Ibrahim - who is not al-Nakha'i - from Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I cannot learn the Qur'an, so teach me something that will suffice me. He said: Say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no deity but Allah, and Allah is Greatest; and there is no power nor strength except by Allah. The Bedouin said: Like this - and clenched his hand. He said: This is for Allah, so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, grant me well-being, provide for me and guide me. The Bedouin took them and clenched both his hands. He said: As for this, he has filled his hands with good."
"525","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from one who heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits it; nor does he drink wine while he is a believer when he drinks it; nor does he steal while he is a believer when he steals it; nor does he plunder a plunder of value or nobility while he is a believer. Shu'bah said: Al-Hakam doubted."
"526","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Ya'fur, from Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: I campaigned - or we campaigned - with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in seven campaigns, eating locusts."
"527","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from al-Qasim, from Ibn Abi Awfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The prayer of the oft-returning (to Allah in devotion) is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun."
"528","Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Mukhtar, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and they were struck by thirst, and they came upon water. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began giving the people drink. They said: O Messenger of Allah, drink, drink, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The pourer of the people is the last of them."
"529","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Warqa, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says eleven times: There is no deity but Allah, alone, without partner, the One, the Eternal, who neither begets nor is born, and there is none like unto Him - Allah will write for him two million good deeds."
"530","Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, saying: Fa'id Abu al-Warqa narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa al-Aslami, who said: I went out and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar were sitting, and a small boy was weeping. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar: Draw the child to you, for he is lost. Umar drew him to himself. While we were sitting, his mother came wailing - I think he said - saying: O my son! and weeping. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar: Call the woman, for she is the mother of the child; she had uncovered her head, with no veil upon it, in distress over her son. She came until she seized the child from the lap of Umar while weeping, with the child in her lap. She turned, and when she saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: How ruined I would be not to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said thereupon: Do you consider this one merciful to her child? His Companions said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; the believer's mercy suffices. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, Allah is more merciful to the believer than this one is to her child."
"531","Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi informed us, saying: Fa'id narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: We saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when morning came he would say: We have entered morning and sovereignty belongs to Allah; and grandeur, greatness, creation, night and day and what rests therein belong to Allah alone, without partner. O Allah, make this day: its beginning rectitude, its middle prosperity and its end success; and I ask You the good of this world and the good of the Hereafter."
"532","Abd al-Rahim ibn Harun al-Wasiti al-Ghassani narrated to us, saying: Fa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: By Allah, while we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a Bedouin came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, intense desire and hunger have destroyed me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bedouin, desire and hunger? He said: That is it. He said: Go, and the first woman you meet who has no husband is your wife. The Bedouin said: So I entered the palm-grove of Banu al-Najjar, and there was a slave-girl gathering dates into a basket. I said to her: O possessor of the basket, do you have a husband? She said: No. I said: Come down, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has married you to me. He said: So she came down, and I went with her to her house, and she said to her father: This Bedouin came to us while I was gathering dates into the basket, and asked me: Do you have a husband? I said: No. He said: Come down, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has married you to me. The father of the slave-girl came out to the Bedouin, and the Bedouin said to him: What is the possessor of the basket to you? He said: My daughter. He said: Does she have a husband? He said: No. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has married her to me. The slave-girl and the father of the slave-girl went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Does she have a husband? He said: No. He said: Go, prepare her trousseau well, then send her to him. The father of the slave-girl went, prepared his daughter, took good care of her, then sent with her dates and milk. She brought them to the house of the Bedouin, and the Bedouin went to his house and saw an adorned slave-girl, and saw dates and milk, so he stood to pray. When dawn broke, he went early to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the father of the slave-girl went early to his daughter, and she said: By Allah, he did not approach us, nor did he approach our dates or our milk. He said: So the father of the slave-girl went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he called the Bedouin and said: O Bedouin, what prevented you from consummating with your wife? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I left your presence and entered the house, and there was an adorned slave-girl, and I saw dates and milk; so it became incumbent upon me for Allah to keep my night alive in worship until morning. He said: O Bedouin, go and consummate with your wife."
"533","Abu Jabir informed us, saying: Fa'id narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: In Medina there was a paralyzed man, and he said to his family: Place me upon the path of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to his mosque. He said: So the paralyzed man was placed upon the path of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the mosque, he would greet the paralyzed man. The family of the paralyzed man came to take him back to his family, and he said: No, by Allah, I will not leave this place as long as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lives; so build for me a reed hut. He said: So they built for him a reed hut, and the paralyzed man remained in it; whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed to the mosque, he would enter the hut and greet the paralyzed man. Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) received a morsel of food, he would send it to the paralyzed man. He said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a caller came and announced to him the death of the paralyzed man. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose, and we rose with him, until when he drew near the hut, he said to his Companions: Let no one approach the hut but me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew near the hut, and Gabriel, peace be upon him, was sitting at the head of the paralyzed man. Gabriel said: O Messenger of Allah, had you not come to us, we would have sufficed you his affair; but since you have come, you are most entitled to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over him, washed him with his hand, shrouded him, prayed over him and placed him in the grave."
"534","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, saying: Ibrahim Abu Isma'il al-Saksaki narrated to me, saying: I heard Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa saying to Yazid ibn Abi Kabshah - and we accompanied one another on a journey, and Ibn Abi Kabshah would fast while traveling - Abu Burdah said: I heard Abu Musa repeatedly say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Muslim man falls ill or travels, there is written for him of reward what he used to do while resident and healthy."
"535","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: al-Jurayri informed us, from Ghunaym ibn Qays al-Tamimi, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of this heart is the likeness of a feather in a desert land, turned over by the wind, back to belly."
"536","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: al-Mas'udi informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Ummah is a nation shown mercy; there is no punishment upon it in the Hereafter - its punishment is in this world: killing, turmoil and earthquakes."
"537","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to me, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Abu Burdah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This Ummah is a nation shown mercy; its punishment is at its own hands. When the Day of Resurrection comes, every man among them will be given a man from the people of dhimmah or from the people of polytheism, and it will be said: This is your ransom from the Fire."
"538","Husayn al-Ju'fi narrated to me, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Thabit ibn Hajjaj al-Kilabi, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from his father: Two men disputed over land, one of them from the people of Hadramawt, and they raised the matter to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He assigned the oath to one of them, and the other cried out and said: He has made it his oath and thereby cuts off my land by his oath. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he cuts off your land by his oath unjustly, he will be among those whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify, and for him is a painful punishment. The other said: Then I do not care. He said: And the other refrained from the oath."
"539","Husayn al-Ju'fi informed us, from Mujammi' ibn Yahya al-Ansari, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: We prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we said: If only we sat until we pray Isha with him. He said: So we sat. He said: He came out to us and said: Have you remained here? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; we said we would pray Isha with you. He said: You have done well - or you are right. He said: Then he raised his head to the sky - and he would often raise his head to the sky - and said: The stars are a safeguard for the sky; when the stars go, there will come to the sky what it is promised. And I am a safeguard for my Companions; when I go, there will come to my Companions what they are promised. And my Companions are a safeguard for my Ummah; when my Companions go, there will come to my Ummah what they are promised."
"540","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Umarah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will gather the nations on the Day of Resurrection upon a single plain. When it pleases Him to separate His creation, there will be presented to every people what they used to worship, and they will follow them until they plunge them into the Fire. Then our Lord will come to us while we are upon an elevated place and say: Who are you? We will say: We are the Muslims. He will say: What are you awaiting? They will say: We are awaiting our Lord, Mighty and Majestic. He will say: And do you know Him if you see Him? They will say: Yes. He will say: How do you know Him when you have not seen Him? They will say: We know Him, that there is no equal to Him. He said: Then our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will manifest Himself laughing, then say: Rejoice, O company of Muslims, for there is none among you except that I have placed in his stead in the Fire a Jew or a Christian."
"541","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hakim ibn al-Daylam, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us with four words and said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not sleep, nor is it befitting for Him to sleep. He lowers the balance and raises it. The deed of the night is raised to Him before the day, and the deed of the day before the night. His veil is fire - were He to uncover it, the splendor of His Face would burn everything His sight reaches."
"542","Husayn al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, who said: Abdullah ibn Qays narrated to me: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we overlooked a valley. He said: The people descended into it, saying: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest; there is no deity but Allah, and Allah is Greatest. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, be gentle with yourselves, for you do not call upon one deaf nor absent; you call upon One All-Hearing, Near - He is with you. He said: So I kept treading the path, saying behind him: There is no power nor strength except by Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abdullah ibn Qays, shall I not guide you to a word from the treasure of Paradise? I said: Yes, may my father and mother be ransom for you. He said: There is no power nor strength except by Allah."
"543","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two Muslims confront one another with their swords and one of them kills the other, both are in the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the killer - but what of the killed? He said: He intended to kill his companion."
"544","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The tent is a pearl, its height in the sky sixty miles; in every corner of it are people for the believer whom the others do not see."
"545","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: Abu Qudamah narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Qays, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gardens of al-Firdaws are four: two of gold, their ornament, their buildings and what is in them; and two of silver, their ornament, their buildings and what is in them. There is nothing between the people and looking at their Lord except the cloak of grandeur upon His Face in the Gardens of Eden. And these are gardens that gush forth from the Gardens of Eden into a hollow, then split thereafter into rivers."
"546","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold and silk are forbidden for the males of my Ummah, lawful for its females."
"547","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"548","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind informed us, from his father, from a man, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plays with knucklebones has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"549","Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, saying: Awf narrated to us, from Qasamah ibn Zuhayr, who said: I heard al-Ash'ari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created Adam from a handful He grasped from the whole earth; so the children of Adam came according to the earth: among them came the red, the white and the black, and between that the soft and the rugged, the wicked and the good."
"550","Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, saying: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to set out with Ja'far ibn Abi Talib to the land of al-Najashi. That reached Quraysh, so they sent Amr ibn al-As and Umarah ibn al-Walid, and gathered a gift for al-Najashi. He said: We arrived, and they arrived before al-Najashi; they brought him their gift and he accepted it, and they prostrated to him. Then Amr ibn al-As said to him: Some people of ours have turned away from our religion and are in your land. Al-Najashi said to them: In my land? They said: Yes. He said: So he sent for us. Ja'far said to us: Let none of you speak; I am your spokesman today. He said: We reached al-Najashi while he was sitting in his assembly, with Amr ibn al-As on his right and Umarah ibn al-Walid on his left, and the priests and monks sitting in two rows. Amr ibn al-As and Umarah ibn al-Walid had told him that they do not prostrate to him. He said: When we reached him we drew near; those of the priests and monks with him said: Prostrate to the king. Ja'far said: We prostrate to none but Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: When we reached al-Najashi, he said: What prevented you from prostrating? He said: We prostrate to none but Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Al-Najashi said to him: And what is that? He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent among us a Messenger - and he is the one whom Jesus son of Mary, peace be upon him, gave glad tidings of: a Messenger to come after me whose name is Ahmad. He commanded us to worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, to establish prayer and give charity, and commanded us to good and forbade us evil. He said: Al-Najashi was impressed by his words. When Amr ibn al-As saw that, he said: May Allah keep the king well, they oppose you concerning the son of Mary. Al-Najashi said to Ja'far: What does your companion say concerning the son of Mary? He said: He says concerning him the word of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: He is the Spirit of Allah and His Word, whom He brought forth from the chaste Virgin whom no human touched. He said: Al-Najashi took a stick from the ground and said: O company of priests and monks, these add nothing to what we say concerning the son of Mary beyond the weight of this. Welcome to you and to him from whom you have come; I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah and that he is the one whom Jesus son of Mary gave glad tidings of. Were it not for the kingship I am in, I would have gone to him to carry his sandals. Remain in my land as long as you wish. And he ordered for us food and clothing, and said: Return to these two their gift. He said: Amr ibn al-As was a short man and Umarah ibn al-Walid was a handsome man. He said: They set out by sea toward al-Najashi, and they drank wine; and with Amr ibn al-As was his wife. When they drank wine, Umarah said: Order your wife to kiss me. Amr said: Have you no shame? Umarah seized Amr and threw him into the sea; Amr kept pleading with Umarah until he brought him into the ship. Amr bore him a grudge for that. Amr said to al-Najashi: When you go out, Umarah stays behind with your family. He said: So al-Najashi summoned Umarah and blew into his urethra, and he went off with the wild beasts."
"551","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, who said: I buried a son of mine while I was in the grave, when Abu Talhah al-Khawlani took my hand and pulled me out. He said: Shall I not give you glad tidings? I said: Yes. He said: Al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Arzarm narrated to me, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah says: O Angel of death, have you taken the child of My servant? He says: Yes. He says: Have you taken the delight of his eye and the fruit of his heart? He says: Yes. He says: So what did he say? He says: He praised You and said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return. He says: Build for him a house in Paradise and name it the House of Praise."
"552","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, saying: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people but has not yet joined them. He said: A person is with whom he loves."
"553","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: al-Thawri informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Musa, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man fights for show, a man fights out of zeal, and a man fights out of courage; so which of that is in the path of Allah? He said: Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is supreme is in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"554","Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sufyan and Isra'il, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed the hungry, visit the sick, and free the captive. Sufyan said: Al-ani is the captive."
"555","Abd al-Razzaq informed us - I am Abd al-Razzaq; Ma'mar informed us - from Qatadah, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - I think he said: in a garden - when a man came and greeted. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go, permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. He said: So I went, and he was Abu Bakr. I said: Enter, and rejoice in Paradise. He kept praising Allah until he sat. Then another came and greeted. He said: Go, permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. I went, and he was Umar. I said: Enter, and rejoice in Paradise. He kept praising Allah until he sat. Then another came and greeted. He said: Go, permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise despite severe tribulation. I went, and it was Uthman. I said: Enter, and rejoice in Paradise despite severe tribulation. He kept saying: O Allah, patience - until he sat."
"556","Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Burdah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Burdah, from his grandfather Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other."
"557","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, saying: Thabit ibn Umarah al-Hanafi narrated to us, saying: I heard Ghunaym ibn Qays say: I heard Abu Musa narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Any woman who perfumes herself and passes by people so they find her scent is an adulteress, and every eye is adulterous."
"558","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: al-Mughirah ibn Abi al-Hurr al-Kindi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while we were sitting and said: Never has a morning come upon me except that I sought Allah's forgiveness therein a hundred times."
"559","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, saying: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, saying: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to me, from al-Muttalib ibn Hantab, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is displeased by his evil deed and pleased by his good deed is a believer."
"560","Zayd ibn Hubab al-Ukli narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold to cow's milk, for it pastures upon every tree. [Continuation of the narration of Abu Musa.]"
"561","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Upon every Muslim is charity. It was said: And if he finds no charity? He said: He works with his hands, benefiting himself and giving charity. It was said: And if he cannot? He said: He helps the needy, distressed one. It was said: And if he cannot? He said: He enjoins good. It was said: And if he cannot do that? He said: He refrains from evil, for that is charity for him."
"562","Abu al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us - Amr said: He informed me - from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, stretches His Hand by night that the evildoer of the day may repent, and stretches His Hand by day that the evildoer of the night may repent, until the sun rises from its setting place."
"563","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, saying: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Tamimah, from Abu Musa, who said: Whoever fasts perpetually, Allah will constrict Hell upon him until it becomes narrower than ninety."
"564","Hammam said: Aban ibn Abi Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Tamimah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. Hammam said: So I said to him: Qatadah did not raise it (to the Prophet). He said: Aban informed me in my house, raised (to the Prophet)."
"565","Abu al-Walid narrated to me, saying: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, who said: Abu Musa al-Ash'ari narrated to us, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The likeness of the believer who recites the Qur'an is the likeness of the citron: its taste is pleasant and its scent pleasant. And the likeness of the believer who does not recite the Qur'an is like the date: its taste is pleasant and it has no scent. And the likeness of the wicked one who recites the Qur'an is like basil: its scent is pleasant and its taste bitter. And the likeness of the wicked one who does not recite the Qur'an is like the colocynth: its taste is bitter and it has no scent."
"566","Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, saying: I heard Murrah al-Hamdani, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Many among men have attained perfection, and among women none attained perfection but Maryam daughter of Imran, and Asiyah wife of Pharaoh; and the superiority of A'ishah over women is like the superiority of tharid over food."
"567","Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, saying: Ulaylah ibn Badr narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two and more constitute a congregation."
"568","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me, saying: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, saying: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to me, from al-Muttalib ibn Hantab, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves his world harms his Hereafter, and whoever loves his Hereafter harms his world; so prefer what remains over what perishes."
"569","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which religions are most beloved to Allah, Mighty and Majestic? He said: The easy, upright monotheism."
"570","Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: al-Mustalim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Abu Ali al-Rahabi narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed from major impurity and saw a spot upon his shoulder that water had not touched. He said: So he wrung his hair over it and wiped it with it."
"571","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ma'iz ibn Malik when he came to him and confessed adultery before him: 'Perhaps you kissed or touched?' He said: No. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Did you have intercourse with her?' He said: Yes. So he ordered that he be stoned."
"572","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: 'The little finger and the thumb are equal.'"
"573","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Abbad ibn Mansur informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a kohl container with which he would apply kohl before sleeping, three times in each eye."
"574","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Abbad ibn Mansur informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: 'The best day on which you perform cupping is the seventeenth, the nineteenth, and the twenty-first.' He said: And I did not pass by any assembly of angels on the night I was taken up except that they said: 'Upon you is cupping, O Muhammad.'"
"575","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: 'Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one to whom it is done; and whomever you find having intercourse with an animal, kill him and kill the animal along with him.'"
"576","Mu'adh ibn Hisham al-Dastawa'i narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said - and I think he attributed it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: 'The donkey, the dog, the menstruating woman, the Jew, the Christian, the Magian, and the pig interrupt the prayer.' He said: And it suffices you, if they are at the distance of a stone's throw from you, they do not interrupt your prayer."
"577","Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam ibn Aban narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Ikrimah, concerning His saying, exalted is He: 'Whom you ask by, and the wombs.' He said: And Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted is He, says: 'Maintain your ties of kinship, for that is more lasting for you in the life of this world and better for you in your Hereafter.'"
"578","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: Thabit ibn Yazid al-Ahwal narrated to us: Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fought an enemy of his, and he did not finish with them until Asr was delayed past its time. When he looked and saw that, he said: 'O Allah, whoever kept us from the middle prayer, fill their hearts with fire and fill their graves with fire.'"
"579","Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi informed us, from Ali ibn Nizar, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Two groups of my Ummah have no share in Islam: the Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah.'"
"580","Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Abu Sa'd al-Baqqal narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My sister vowed to walk to the House, and it is hard for her to walk. He said: 'Command her to ride if she cannot walk, for Allah has no need to burden your sister with hardship.'"
"581","Uthman ibn Umar informed us: Hisham informed us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while his armor was pawned with a man for twenty Sa' of barley which he had taken as food for his family."
"582","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Asim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, he stayed twenty nights shortening the prayer."
"583","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Yazid al-Madani narrating from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: There is no recitation in Zuhr and Asr. It was said to him: People do recite. He said: If I had authority over them I would cut off their tongues. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited, so his recitation is recitation for us; and he was silent, so his silence is silence."
"584","Abu al-Walid narrated to me: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to me, from Humayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah bint al-Harith while both were in ihram."
"585","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Makkah after the conquest for seventeen days, praying two rak'ahs."
"586","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: 'He is not of us who does not show mercy to our young, honor our elder, enjoin good, and forbid evil.'"
"587","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Nusayr ibn Dha'luq, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while his armor was pawned with a Jew for thirty Sa' of barley."
"588","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: 'Sacrifice has been prescribed for me but not prescribed for you, and I have been commanded to pray Duha but you have not been commanded to do so.'"
"589","Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Bajali narrated to me, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, he said: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Allah has cursed whoever changes the boundary marks of the land; Allah has cursed whoever takes loyalty to other than his patrons; Allah has cursed whoever leads a blind man astray from the path; Allah has cursed whoever curses his parents; Allah has cursed whoever slaughters for other than Allah; Allah has cursed whoever commits bestiality; Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut' - then 'Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut' - then 'Allah has cursed whoever does the deed of the people of Lut.'"
"590","Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to me: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, he said: Amr ibn Abi Amr narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Bathing on Friday is not obligatory, but whoever bathes, it is better and purer. Then he said: People at the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear wool, and the mosque was narrow with a low roof. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one Friday on a hot summer day of intense heat, and his pulpit was small, only three steps. He addressed the people, and the people sweated in their wool, so the smell of sweat and wool rose until they almost harmed one another, until their odor reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on the pulpit. He said: 'O people, when this day comes, bathe, and let each of you apply the best perfume or oil he can find.'"
"591","Amr ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to me: al-Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A mouse came and began dragging the wick. The slave girl went to chase it away, but the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Leave it.' So it brought it and threw it before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the mat on which he was sitting, and it burned an area of it the size of a dirham. He said: 'When you sleep, extinguish your lamps, for Satan guides one like this to this, and it burns you.'"
"592","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would spend nights hungry with an empty stomach while his family found no supper, and most of their bread was barley bread."
"593","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Zayd - brother of Hammad ibn Zayd - narrated to us: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abbas used to say: Memorize this hadith: One of the daughters of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was dying, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed her on his hands and put her head between his hands while she was in her death throes until she passed away, and he laid her down while weeping. Umm Ayman cried out, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Do I see you weeping in the presence of the Messenger of Allah?' She said: Do I not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping? He said: 'I weep, and it is mercy. The believer is in good in every state; his soul is taken from between his sides while he praises Allah, mighty and exalted is He.'"
"594","Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Bajali narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Isma'il narrated to me, he said: Dawud ibn Husayn narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us a supplication against all pains and fever, saying: 'In the name of Allah, the Great. I seek refuge with Allah, the Almighty, from the evil of a spurting vein and from the heat of the Fire.'"
"595","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to me: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he was asked about prostration in Sad. He said: It is not among the obligatory prostrations, but I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating in it."
"596","Al-Qa'nabi narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: A man seized his debtor for ten dinars and said to him: By Allah, I have nothing with which to pay you today. He said: By Allah, I will not leave you until you pay me or bring me a guarantor to guarantee for you. He said: By Allah, I have no payment and I find no one to guarantee for me. He said: So he dragged him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this man seized me, and I asked him for a respite of one month, but he refused unless I pay him or bring a guarantor. I said: By Allah, I find no guarantor and I have no payment today. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'Will you grant respite for only one month?' He said: No. He said: 'Then I will guarantee it for him.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) guaranteed it for him. The man went and brought him the amount at the promised time. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'From where did you get this gold?' He said: From a mine. He said: 'Go, we have no need of it; there is no good in it.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid it off on his behalf."
"597","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Ilba ibn Ahmar, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew four lines, then said: 'Do you know what this is?' They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The best women of Paradise are Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah the daughter of Muhammad, Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh.'"
"598","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: Thabit ibn Yazid al-Ahwal narrated to us: Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned toward Uhud and said: 'By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, it would not please me if Uhud were turned into gold for the family of Muhammad which I would spend in the cause of Allah, mighty and exalted is He, and I die on the day I die leaving two dinars of it except two dinars I set aside for a debt, if there is any.' He said: Then he died leaving neither dinar nor dirham, neither male nor female slave, and he left his armor pawned with a Jew for thirty Sa' of barley."
"599","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us: Hilal ibn Khabbab narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Umar entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a mat that had left marks on his side. He said to him: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would take a bed softer than this! He said: 'What have I to do with this world? What have I to do with this world? By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, my example and the example of this world is but that of a rider who traveled on a hot summer day, then shaded himself under a tree for an hour of the day, then moved on and left it.'"
"600","Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When you differ about the road, make it seven cubits wide.'"
